    'definition': '<b>AB</b>, <i>In</i> English names, is an abbreviation of Abbey or Abbot.<br><br><b>AB</b>, <i>a</i> prefix to words of Latin origin, and a Latin preposition, as in abscond, written in ancient Latin af. It denotes from, separating or departure.<br><br><b>AB</b>, <i>The</i> Hebrew name of Father.<br><br><b>AB</b>, <i>The</i> eleventh month of the Jewish civil year, and fifth of the ecclesiastical year, answering to a part of July, and a part of August.',
