  'Betroth': {
    'id': 5788,
    'definition': '<b>BETROTH\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [be and troth, truth, faith. See <a href="dict://Truth,">Truth,</a> and Troth.]<br><br>1. To contract to any one, in order to a future marriage; to promise or pledge one to be the future spouse of another; to affiance; used of either sex. "The father betroths his daughter.\'<br><br>2. To contract with one for a future spouse; to espouse; as, a man betroths a lady.<br><br>3. To nominate to a bishopric,in order to consecration.',
  },
