    'definition': '<b>BOM\'BIC</b>, <i>a.</i> [L.bombyx, a silk worm.]<br><br>Pertaining to the silk worm; as bombic acid.',
  },
  'Bombilation': {
    'id': 6550,
    'definition': '<b>BOMBILA\'TION</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. bombilo.] Sound; report; noise. [Little used.]<br><br><b>BOMB\'-KETCH<br><br>BOMB\'-VESSEL</b>, <i>n.</i> A small ship or vessel, constructed for throwing bombs into a fortress from the sea, and built remarkably strong, in order to sustain the shocks produced by the discharge of the mortars. They generally are rigged as ketches.',
  },
  'Bombycinous': {
    'id': 6551,
    'definition': '<b>BOMBYC\'INOUS</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. bombycinus, from bombyx, a silk worm.]<br><br>1. Silken; made of silk.<br><br>2. Being of the color of the silk worm; transparent, with a yellow tint.',
