  'Bourgeon': {
    'id': 6772,
    'definition': '<b>BOUR\'GEON</b>, <i>v.i.</i> bur\'jun. To sprout; to put forth buds; to shoot forth as a branch.',
  },
  'Bourn': {
    'id': 6773,
    'definition': '<b>BOURN</b>, <i>rather</i> <b>BORNE</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. A bound; a limit.<br><br>That undiscovered country, from whose bourn<br><br>No traveller returns.-------<br><br>2. A brook; a torrent; a rivulet. [In this sense obsolete; but retained in many names of towns, seated on the banks of streams. In Scotland, it is still used in the sense of a brook, but they write it burn.]',
