    'definition': '<b>BOW-DYE</b>, <i>n.</i> A kind of scarlet color, superior to madder, but inferior to the true scarlet grain for fixedness, and duration; first used at Bow, near London.<br><br><b>BOW\'-GRACE</b>, <i>n.</i> In sea language, a frame or composition of junk, laid out at the sides, stem, or bows of ships to secure them from injury by ice.',
