  'Breakwater': {
    'id': 6995,
    'definition': '<b>BREAKWATER</b>, <i>n.</i> [break and water.] The hull of an old vessel sunk at the entrance of a harbor, to break or diminish the force of the waves, to secure the vessels in harbor.<br><br>1. A small buoy fastened to a large one, when the rope of the latter is not long enough to reach the surface of the water.<br><br>2. A mole, at the mouth of a harbor, intended to break the force of the waves.',
