  'Breccia': {
    'id': 7020,
    'definition': '<b>BREC\'CIA</b>, <i>n.</i> In mineralogy, an aggregate composed of angular fragments of the same mineral, or of different minerals, united by a cement, and presenting a variety of colors. Sometimes a few of the fragments are a little rounded. The varieties are the siliceous, calcarious and trap breccias.<br><br>When rounded stones and angular fragments are united by a cement, the aggregate is usually called coarse conglomerate.',
