    'definition': '<b>BRUS\'TLING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Crackling; rustling; vaporing.',
  },
  'Brut': {
    'id': 7307,
    'definition': '<b>BRUT</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To browse. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Brutal': {
    'id': 7308,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TAL</b>, <i>a.</i> [See <a href="dict://Brute">Brute</a>.] Pertaining to a brute; as brutal nature.<br><br>1. Savage; cruel; inhuman; brutish; unfeeling like a brute; merciless; as brutal courage; brutal manners.',
  },
  'Brutality': {
    'id': 7309,
    'definition': '<b>BRUTAL\'ITY</b>, <i>n.</i> Inhumanity; savageness; churlishness; insensibility to pity or shame.',
  },
  'Brutalize': {
    'id': 7310,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TALIZE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To make brutal, churlish or inhuman.<br><br>All cruel punishments brutalize the heart.<br><br><b>BRU\'TALIZE</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To become brutal, inhuman, or coarse and beastly.',
  },
  'Brutally': {
    'id': 7311,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TALLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> Cruelly; inhumanly; in a coarse, churlish, or brutal manner.',
  },
  'Brute': {
    'id': 7312,
    'definition': '<b>BRUTE</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. brutus, senseless,irrational.]<br><br>1. Senseless; unconscious; as the brute earth.<br><br>2. Irrational; ferine; as a brute beast.<br><br>3. Bestial; in common with beasts; as brute violence.<br><br>4. Rough; uncivilized; insensible; as a brute philosopher.<br><br><b>BRUTE</b>, <i>n.</i> A beast; any animal destitute of reason, and of course the word comprehends all animals except man, but is applied mostly to the larger beasts.<br><br>1. A brutal person; a savage in heart or manners; a low bred,unfeeling man.<br><br><b>BRUTE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> for bruit, to report. [Not used.]',
  },
  'Brutely': {
    'id': 7313,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TELY</b>, <i>adv.</i> In a rude manner.',
  },
  'Bruteness': {
    'id': 7314,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TENESS</b>, <i>n.</i> Brutality.',
  },
  'Brutify': {
    'id': 7315,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TIFY</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To make a person a brute; to make senseless, stupid or unfeeling.',
  },
  'Brutish': {
    'id': 7316,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TISH</b>, <i>a.</i> Like a brute or beast; as a brutish form.<br><br>1. Insensible; stupid; as brutish men.<br><br>2. Unfeeling; savage; ferocious; brutal.<br><br>3. Gross; carnal; bestial.<br><br>4. Ignorant; uncivilized; untaught.',
  },
  'Brutishly': {
    'id': 7317,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TISHLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> In the manner of a brute; grossly; irrationally; stupidly; savagely.',
  },
  'Brutishness': {
    'id': 7318,
    'definition': '<b>BRU\'TISHNESS</b>, <i>n.</i> Stupidity; insensibility; brutality; savageness; the qualities of a brute.',
  },
  'Brutism': {
    'id': 7319,
    'definition': '<b>BRUTISM</b>, <i>n.</i> The nature or characteristic qualitites or actions of a brute; extreme stupidity or beastly vulgarity.',
  },
  'Bryony': {
    'id': 7320,
    'definition': '<b>BRY\'ONY</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. bryonia.] White jalap; a genus of plants of several species. The root of the rough or white bryony is a strong irritating cathartic.<br><br>Black-bryony is a genus of plants, called Tamus.',
  },
  'Bub': {
    'id': 7321,
    'definition': '<b>BUB</b>, <i>n.</i> A cant word for strong malt liquor.<br><br><b>BUB</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To throw out in bubbles. [Not used.]',
  },
  'Bubble': {
    'id': 7322,
    'definition': '<b>BUB\'BLE</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. A small bladder or vesicle of water or other fluid inflated with air.<br><br>2. Any thing that wants firmness or solidity; a vain project; that which is more specious than real. Hence, a false show; a cheat or fraud.<br><br>3. A delusive scheme of speculation; an empty project to raise money or imaginary grounds; as the South Sea bubble.<br><br>4. A person deceived by an empty project.<br><br><b>BUB\'BLE</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To rise in bubbles, as liquors when boiling or agitated.<br><br>1. To run with a gurgling noise; as a bubbling stream.<br><br><b>BUB\'BLE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To cheat; to deceive or impose on.',
  },
  'Bubbler': {
    'id': 7323,
    'definition': '<b>BUB\'BLER</b>, <i>n.</i> One who cheats.',
  },
  'Bubby': {
    'id': 7324,
    'definition': '<b>BUB\'BY</b>, <i>n.</i> [from the same root as bubble and bubo.] A woman\'s breast.',
  },
  'Bubo': {
    'id': 7325,
    'definition': '<b>BU\'BO</b>,n. [L. bubo, a swelling.] A tumor or abscess with inflammation, which rises in certain glandular parts of the body, as in the groin, or armpit.',
  },
  'Bubonocele': {
    'id': 7326,
    'definition': '<b>BU\'BONOCELE</b>, <i>n.</i> [Gr.the groin, and a tumor.] Hernia inguinalis, or inguinal rupture; a tumor in the groin, formed by a prolapsus of the intestines or omentum or both, through the processes of the peritoneum and rings of the abdominal muscles.',
  },
  'Bubukle': {
    'id': 7327,
    'definition': '<b>BU\'BUKLE</b>, <i>n.</i> A red pimple. [Not used.]',
  },
  'Bubulca': {
    'id': 7328,
    'definition': '<b>BUBUL\'CA</b>, <i>n.</i> A flat fresh-water fish, of a circular form and a silvery color.',
  },
  'Bucaneer': {
    'id': 7329,
    'definition': '<b>BUCANEE\'R,<br><br>BUCANIE\'R</b>, <i>n.</i> Primarily, a buccaneer is said to one who dries and smokes flesh or fish after the manner of the Indians. The name was first given to the French settlers in Haiti or Hispaniola, whose business was to hunt wild cattle and swine. It was afterwards applied to the piratical adventurers, English and French, who combined to make depredations on the Spaniards in America.',
  },
  'Bucao': {
    'id': 7330,
    'definition': '<b>BUCA\'O</b>, <i>n.</i> A species of owl, in the Philippine isles, of a beautiful plumage, and size of a peacock, but remarkable for a hideous nocturnal scream.',
  },
  'Buccal': {
    'id': 7331,
    'definition': '<b>BUC\'CAL</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. bucca, the cheek.] Pertaining to the cheek. The buccal glands are the small glands of the mouth,under the cheek, which secrete saliva.',
  },
  'Buccellation': {
    'id': 7332,
    'definition': '<b>BUCCELLA\'TION</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. buccella, buccea, a mouthful.]<br><br>The act of breaking into large pieces.',
  },
  'Buccinite': {
    'id': 7333,
    'definition': '<b>BUC\'CINITE</b>, <i>n.</i> Fossil remains or petrifactions of the shells called buccinum.',
  },
  'Bucentaur': {
    'id': 7334,
    'definition': '<b>BUCENT\'AUR</b>, <i>n.</i> The state barge of Venice.',
  },
  'Bucephalus': {
