  'Buzz': {
    'id': 7625,
    'definition': '<b>BUZZ</b>, <i>v.i.<br><br></i> 1. To make a low hissing sound, as bees; to make the sound of z, with an expiration of breath between the tongue and the roof of the mouth or upper teeth.<br><br>2. To whisper; to speak with a low hissing voice; to make a low hissing sound.<br><br><b>BUZZ</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To whisper; to spread, as report, by whispers, or to spread secretly.<br><br><b>BUZZ</b>, <i>n.</i> The noise of bees; also,a whisper.',
  },
  'Buzzard': {
    'id': 7626,
    'definition': '<b>BUZZ\'ARD</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. A species of falco, or hawk,the buteo; a rapacious,but sluggish bird; the breast usually of a yellowish white; the upper parts of a deep brown. In some parts of America, it is called the great Hen-hawk, from its feeding on poultry.<br><br>2. A block-head; a dunce.<br><br><b>BUZZ\'ARD</b>, <i>a.</i> Senseless; stupid.',
  },
  'Buzzardet': {
    'id': 7627,
    'definition': '<b>BUZZARDET\'</b>, <i>n.</i> A species of Falco or hawk, resembling the buzzard in most respects; but its legs are in proportion rather longer.',
  },
  'Buzzer': {
    'id': 7628,
    'definition': '<b>BUZZ\'ER</b>, <i>n.</i> A whisperer; one who is busy in telling tales secretly.',
