  'Byssolite': {
    'id': 7643,
    'definition': '<b>BYS\'SOLITE</b>,n. [Gr. fine flax, and stone; so called from its resemblance to moss.]<br><br>A rare mineral, occurring in very delicate filaments, short, flexible and elastic. Their color is olive green, or brownish yellow, and their luster a little silky. Jameson places byssolite under actinolite; Hauy arranges it under amianthoid.<br><br><b>BYS\'SUS</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. byssus; Gr. fine linen, or cotton.]<br><br>The asbestus, composed of parallel fibers,is by some called by this name.',
