  'Caboched': {
    'id': 7679,
    'definition': '<b>CABOCHED,<br><br>CABOOSE</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. The cook-room or kitchen of a ship. In smaller vessels, it is an inclosed fire-place, hearth or stove for cooking, on the main deck. In a ship of war, the cook room is called a galley.<br><br>2. A box that covers the chimney in a ship.',
