    'definition': '<b>CANNEL-COAL or CANDLE-COAL</b>, <i>n.</i> A hard, opake, inflammable fossil coal of a black color, sufficiently solid to be cut and polished. On fire it decrepitates and breaks into angular fragments. It is sometimes used for inkholders and toys.',
