    'definition': '<b>CARLINE-THISTLE</b>, <i>n.</i> A genus of plants growing in the south of France, and one a native of Great Britain.',
  },
  'Carling': {
    'id': 8268,
    'definition': '<b>CARLING</b>, <i>n.</i> A piece of timber in a ship, ranging fore and aft, from one deck beam to another, directly over the keel, serving as a foundation for the body of the ship. On these rest the ledges, on which the planks of the deck are made fast.<br><br>Carline-knees are timbers in a ship, lying across from the sides to the hatchway, and serving to sustain the deck.',
