  'Chasten': {
    'id': 9116,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTEN</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To correct by punishment; to punish; to inflict pain for the purpose of reclaiming an offender; as, to chasten a son with a rod.<br><br>I will chasten him with the rod of men. 2 Sam 7.<br><br>2. To afflict by other means.<br><br>As many as I love I rebuke and chasten. Rev 3.<br><br>3. To purify from errors or faults.',
