  'Chastening': {
    'id': 9120,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTENING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Correcting; afflicting for correction.<br><br><b>CHASTENING</b>, <i>n.</i> Correction; punishment for the purpose of reclaiming.<br><br>No chastening for the present seemeth to be joyous but grievous. Heb 12.',
  },
  'Chastisable': {
    'id': 9121,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTISABLE</b>, <i>a.</i> Deserving of chastisement.',
  },
  'Chastise': {
    'id': 9122,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTISE</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To correct by punishing; to punish; to inflict pain by stripes, or in other manner, for the purpose of punishing an offender and recalling him to his duty.<br><br>I will chastise you seven times for your sins. Lev 26.<br><br>2. To reduce to order or obedience; to restrain; to awe; to repress.<br><br>The gay social sense, By decency chastisd.<br><br>3. To correct; to purify by expunging faults; as, to chastise a poem.',
  },
  'Chastised': {
    'id': 9123,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTISED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Punished; corrected.',
  },
  'Chastisement': {
    'id': 9124,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTISEMENT</b>, <i>n.</i> Correction; punishment; pain inflicted for punishment and correction, either by stripes or otherwise.<br><br>Shall I so much dishonour my fair stars, On equal terms to give him chastisement.<br><br>I have borne chastisement, I will not offend any more. Job 34.<br><br>The chastisement of our peace, in Scripture, was the pain which Christ suffered to purchase our peace and reconciliation to God. Isa 53.',
  },
  'Chastiser': {
    'id': 9125,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTISER</b>, <i>n.</i> One who chastises; a punisher; a corrector.',
  },
  'Chastising': {
    'id': 9126,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTISING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Punishing for correction; correcting.',
  },
  'Chastity': {
    'id': 9127,
    'definition': '<b>CHASTITY</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. Purity of the body; freedom from all unlawful commerce of sexes. Before marriage, purity from all commerce of sexes; after marriage, fidelity to the marriage bed.<br><br>2. Freedom from obscenity, as in language or conversation.<br><br>3. Freedom from bad mixture; purity in words and phrases.<br><br>4. Purity; unadulterated state; as the chastity of the gospel.',
  },
  'Chat': {
    'id': 9128,
    'definition': '<b>CHAT</b>, <i>v.i.<br><br></i> 1. To talk in a familiar manner; to talk without form or ceremony.<br><br>2. To talk idly; to prate.<br><br><b>CHAT</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To talk of.<br><br><b>CHAT</b>, <i>n.</i> Free, familiar talk; idle talk; prate.<br><br><b>CHAT</b>, <i>n.</i> A twig, or little stick. [See <a href="dict://Chit">Chit</a>.]',
  },
  'Chateau': {
