  'Checky': {
    'id': 9168,
    'definition': '<b>CHECKY</b>, <i>n.</i> In heraldry, a border that has more than two rows of checkers, or when the bordure or shield is checkered, like a chess-board.',
  },
  'Cheek': {
    'id': 9169,
    'definition': '<b>CHEEK</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. The side of the face below the eyes on each side.<br><br>2. Among mechanics, cheeks are those pieces of a machine which form corresponding sides, or which are double and alike; as the cheeks of a printing press, which stand perpendicular and support the three sommers, the head, shelves and winter; the cheeks of a turners lathe; the cheeks of a glaziers vise; the cheeks of a mortar, and of a gun-carriage; the cheeks of a mast, which serve to sustain the trestle trees, &c.<br><br>Cheek by jowl, closeness, proximity.',
  },
  'Cheek-Bone': {
    'id': 9170,
    'definition': '<b>CHEEK-BONE</b>, <i>n.</i> The bone of the cheek.',
  },
  'Cheek-Tooth': {
    'id': 9171,
    'definition': '<b>CHEEK-TOOTH</b>, <i>n.</i> The hinder tooth or tusk. Joel 1:6.',
