  'Chew': {
    'id': 9252,
    'definition': '<b>CHEW</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To bite and grind with the teeth; to masticate, as food, to prepare it for deglutition and digestion.<br><br>2. To ruminate in the thoughts; to meditate; as, to chew revenge.<br><br>3. To champ; to bite, hold or roll about in the mouth; as, to chew tobacco.<br><br>4. To taste, without swallowing.<br><br><b>CHEW</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To champ upon; to ruminate.<br><br>Old politicians chew on wisdom past.<br><br><b>CHEW</b>, <i>n.</i> That which is chewed; that which is held in the mouth at once; a cud.',
  },
  'Chewed': {
    'id': 9253,
    'definition': '<b>CHEWED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Ground by the teeth; masticated.',
  },
  'Chewet': {
    'id': 9254,
    'definition': '<b>CHEWET</b>, <i>n.</i> A kind of pie, made with chopped substances.',
