    'definition': '<b>CHICHLING</b>,<br><br><b>CHICK</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To sprout, as seed in the ground; to vegetate.',
  },
  'Chick-Pea': {
    'id': 9265,
    'definition': '<b>CHICK-PEA</b>, <i>n.</i> A plant or pea, constituting the genus Cicer; a native of Spain, where it is used in olios. It is smaller than the common pea.',
  },
  'Chick-Weed': {
    'id': 9266,
    'definition': '<b>CHICK-WEED</b>, <i>n.</i> A plant of the genus Alsine, which includes many species. The common chick-weed, with white blossoms, affords a remarkable instance of the sleep of plants; for, at night, the leaves approach in pairs, and inclose the tender rudiments of the young shoots. The leaves are cooling and nutritive, and are deemed excellent food for persons of a consumptive habit. They are deemed useful also for swelled breasts.',
  },
  'Chicken': {
    'id': 9267,
    'definition': '<b>CHICKEN</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. The young of fowls, particularly of the domestic hen, or gallinaceous fowls.<br><br>2. A person of tender years.<br><br>3. A word of tenderness.',
  },
  'Chicken-Hearted': {
    'id': 9268,
    'definition': '<b>CHICKEN-HEARTED</b>, <i>a.</i> Timid; fearful; cowardly.',
