  'Chinse': {
    'id': 9350,
    'definition': '<b>CHINSE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> In naval affairs, to thrust oakum into the seams or chinks of a ship with a chisel or point of a knife, as a temporary expedient for calking.',
  },
  'Chints': {
    'id': 9351,
    'definition': '<b>CHINTS</b>, <i>n.</i> Cotton cloth, printed with more than two colors.',
  },
  'Chioppine': {
    'id': 9352,
    'definition': '<b>CHIOPPINE</b>, <i>n.</i> A high shoe, formerly worn by ladies.',
  },
  'Chip': {
    'id': 9353,
    'definition': '<b>CHIP, CHEAP, CHIPPING</b>, <i>in</i> the names of places, imply a market; from Sax. Ceapan, cypan, to buy or sell. [See <a href="dict://Cheap">Cheap</a>.]<br><br><b>CHIP</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. A piece of wood or other substance, separated from a body by cutting instrument, particularly by an ax. It is used also for a piece of stone separated by a chisel or other instrument, in hewing.<br><br>2. A fragment or piece broken off; a small piece.<br><br><b>CHIP</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To cut into small pieces, or chips; to diminish by cutting away a little at a time, or in small pieces; to hew.<br><br><b>CHIP</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To break or fly off in small pieces, as in potters ware.',
  },
  'Chip-Ax': {
    'id': 9354,
    'definition': '<b>CHIP-AX</b>, <i>n.</i> An ax for chipping.',
  },
  'Chipped': {
    'id': 9355,
    'definition': '<b>CHIPPED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Cut in chips, or small pieces; hewed.',
  },
  'Chipping': {
    'id': 9356,
    'definition': '<b>CHIPPING</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. A chip; a piece cut off or separated by a cutting or engraving instrument; a fragment.<br><br>2. The flying or breaking off in small pieces, of the edges of potters ware, and porcelain.',
  },
  'Chiragrical': {
    'id': 9357,
    'definition': '<b>CHIRAGRICAL</b>, <i>a.</i> Having the gout in the hand, or subject to that disease.',
  },
  'Chirk': {
    'id': 9358,
    'definition': '<b>CHIRK</b>, <i>a.</i> Lively; cheerful; in god spirits; in a comfortable state.<br><br><b>CHIRK</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To chirp.',
  },
  'Chirm': {
    'id': 9359,
    'definition': '<b>CHIRM</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To sing as a bird.',
  },
  'Chirograph': {
    'id': 9360,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROGRAPH</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. Anciently a deed, which, requiring a counterpart, was engrossed twice on the same piece of parchment, with a space between, in which was written chirograph, through which the parchment was cut, and one part given to each party. It answered to what is now called a charter-party.<br><br>2. A fine, so called from the manner of engrossing, which is still retained in the chirographers office in England.',
  },
  'Chirographer': {
    'id': 9361,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROGRAPHER</b>, <i>n.</i> [See <a href="dict://Chirograph">Chirograph</a>.] He that exercises or professes the art or business of writing. In England, the chirographer of fines is an officer in the common pleas, who engrosses fines acknowledged in that court, and delivers the indentures to the parties.',
  },
  'Chirographic': {
    'id': 9362,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROGRAPHIC,<br><br>CHIROGRAPHICAL</b>, <i>a.</i> Pertaining to chirography.',
  },
  'Chirographist': {
    'id': 9363,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROGRAPHIST</b>, <i>n.</i> One who tells fortunes by examining the hand.',
  },
  'Chirography': {
    'id': 9364,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROGRAPHY</b>, <i>n.</i> [See <a href="dict://Chirograph">Chirograph</a>.] The art of writing, or a writing with ones own hand.',
  },
  'Chirological': {
    'id': 9365,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROLOGICAL</b>, <i>a.</i> Pertaining to chirology.',
  },
  'Chirologist': {
    'id': 9366,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROLOGIST</b>, <i>n.</i> One who communicates thoughts by signs made with the hands and fingers.',
  },
  'Chirology': {
    'id': 9367,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROLOGY</b>, <i>n.</i> [See <a href="dict://Chirologist">Chirologist</a>.] The art or practice of communicating thoughts by signs made by the hands and fingers; a substitute for language or discourse, much used by the deaf and dumb, and by others who communicate with them.',
  },
  'Chiromancer': {
    'id': 9368,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROMANCER</b>, <i>n.</i> [See <a href="dict://Chiromancy">Chiromancy</a>.] One who attempts to foretell future events, or to tell the fortunes and dispositions of persons, by inspecting the hands.',
  },
  'Chiromancy': {
    'id': 9369,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROMANCY</b>, <i>n.</i> Divination by the hand; the art or practice of attempting to foretell events, or to discover the dispositions of a person, by inspecting the lines and lineaments of his hand.',
  },
  'Chiromantic': {
    'id': 9370,
    'definition': '<b>CHIROMANTIC</b>, <i>a.</i> Pertaining to chiromancy, or divination by the hand.<br><br>Chiromantic deception.',
  },
  'Chirp': {
    'id': 9371,
    'definition': '<b>CHIRP</b>, <i>v.i.</i> Cherp. To make the noise of certain small birds, or of certain insects; as a chirping lark, or cricket.<br><br><b>CHIRP</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To make cheerful.<br><br><b>CHIRP</b>, <i>n.</i> A particular voice of certain birds or insects.',
  },
  'Chirper': {
    'id': 9372,
    'definition': '<b>CHIRPER</b>, <i>n.</i> One that chirps, or is cheerful.',
