  'Clause': {
    'id': 9898,
    'definition': '<b>CLAUSE</b>, <i>n.</i> s as z. Literally, a close, or inclosure. Hence, that which is included, or contained, within certain limits.<br><br>1. In language or grammar, a member of a period or sentence; a subdivision of a sentence, in which the words are inseparably connected with each other in sense, and cannot, with propriety, be separated by a point; as, there is reason to think that he afterwards rose to favor, and obtained several honors civil and military. In this sentence are two clauses.<br><br>2. An article in a contract or other writing; a distinct part of a contract, will, agreement, charter, commission, or other writing; a distinct stipulation, condition, proviso, grant, covenant, &c.',
  },
  'Claustral': {
    'id': 9899,
    'definition': '<b>CLAUSTRAL</b>, <i>a.</i> [See <a href="dict://Clause">Clause</a>.] Relating to a cloister, or religious house; as a claustral prior.',
  },
  'Clausure': {
    'id': 9900,
    'definition': '<b>CLAUSURE</b>, <i>n.</i> s as z. [See <a href="dict://Clause">Clause</a>.]<br><br>1. The act of shutting up or confining; confinement.<br><br>2. In anatomy, an imperforated canal.',
