  'Clavichord': {
    'id': 9905,
    'definition': '<b>CLAVICHORD</b>, <i>n.</i> A musical instrument of an oblong figure, of the nature of a spinet. The strings are muffled with small bits of fine woolen cloth, to soften the sounds; used in nunneries. [See <a href="dict://Clarichord">Clarichord</a>.]',
  },
  'Clavicle': {
    'id': 9906,
    'definition': '<b>CLAVICLE</b>, <i>n.</i> The collar bone. There are two clavicles, or channel bones, joined at one end to the scapula or shoulder bone, and at the other, to the sternum or breast bone.',
