  'Cobweb': {
    'id': 10316,
    'definition': '<b>COBWEB</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. The line, thread or filament which a spider spins from its abdomen; the net-work spread by a spider to catch its prey. Hence,<br><br>2. Any snare, implying insidiousness and weakness.<br><br>In this sense it is used adjectively or in composition, for thin, flimsy; as a cobweb law.<br><br>Or slender, feeble; as the cobweb thread of life.',
