  'Collogue': {
    'id': 10595,
    'definition': '<b>COLLOGUE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To wheedle.',
  },
  'Collop': {
    'id': 10596,
    'definition': '<b>COLLOP</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. A small slice of meat; a piece of flesh.<br><br>2. In burlesque, a child.<br><br>In Job 15:27 it seems to have the sense of a thick piece or fleshy lump. He maketh collops of fat on his flanks. This is the sense of the word in N. England.',
