    'definition': '<b>COMPATRIOT</b>, <i>n.</i> A fellow patriot; one of the same country.<br><br><b>COMPATRIOT</b>, <i>a.</i> Of the same country.',
  },
  'Compeer': {
    'id': 10931,
    'definition': '<b>COMPEER</b>, <i>n.</i> An equal; a companion; an associate; a mate.<br><br><b>COMPEER</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To equal; to match; to be equal with.',
  },
  'Compel': {
    'id': 10932,
    'definition': '<b>COMPEL</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To drive or urge with force, or irresistibly; to constrain; to oblige; to necessitate, either by physical or moral force.<br><br>Thou shalt not compel him to serve as a bound servant. Lev 25.<br><br>And they compel one Simon--to bear his cross. Mark 15.<br><br>Go out into the highways and hedges, and compel them to come in, that my house may be filled. Luke 14.<br><br>Circumstances compel us to practice economy.<br><br>2. To force; to take by force, or violence; to seize.<br><br>The subjects grief comes through commissions, which compel from each a sixth part of his substance.<br><br>3. To drive together; to gather; to unite in a crowd or company. A Latinism, compellere gregem.<br><br>In one troop compelled.<br><br>4. To seize; to overpower; to hold.<br><br>And easy sleep their weary limbs compelled.<br><br>5. To call forth, L. compeller.',
  },
