  'Defray': {
    'id': 14435,
    'definition': '<b>DEFRAY</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To pay; to discharge, as cost or expense; to bear, as charge, cost or expense. It is followed chiefly by expense, charge or cost. The acquisitions of war seldom defray the expenses. The profits of a voyage will not always defray the charges, or even the cost of the first outfits.<br><br>2. To satisfy; as, to defray anger.<br><br>3. To fill; as, to defray a bottle.',
  },
  'Defrayed': {
