  'Depletion': {
    'id': 14848,
    'definition': '<b>DEPLETION</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. To fill.] The act of emptying; particularly, in the medical art, the act of diminishing the quantity of blood in the vessels by venesection; bloodletting.',
  },
  'Deplorable': {
    'id': 14849,
    'definition': '<b>DEPLORABLE</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. That may be deplored or lamented; lamentable; that demands or causes lamentation; hence, sad; calamitous; grievous; miserable; wretched; as, the evils of life are deplorable; the Pagan world is in a deplorable condition.<br><br>Deplorate, in a like sense, is not used.<br><br>2. In popular use, low; contemptible; pitiable; as deplorable stupidity.',
  },
  'Deplorableness': {
    'id': 14850,
    'definition': '<b>DEPLORABLENESS</b>, <i>n.</i> The state of being deplorable; misery; wretchedness; a miserable state.',
