    'definition': '<b>DICHOTOMY</b>, <i>n.</i> [Gr., a division into two parts; to cut.]<br><br>1. Division or distribution of ideas by pairs. [Little used.]<br><br>2. In astronomy, that phase of the moon in which it appears bisected, or shows only half its disk, as at the quadratures.',
