  },
  'Dregs': {
    'id': 17413,
    'definition': '<b>DREGS</b>, <i>n.</i> Plu. [Gr.]<br><br>1. The sediment of liquors; lees; grounds; feculence; any foreign matter of liquors that subsides to the bottom of a vessel.<br><br>2. Waste or worthless matter; dross; sweepings; refuse. Hence, the most vile and despicable part of men; as the dregs of society.<br><br>Dreg, in the singular, is found in Spenser, but is not now used.',
