    'definition': '<b>ENLU\'MINE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To illumine; to enlighten. [See <a href="dict://the">the</a> latter words.]',
  },
  'Enmarble': {
    'id': 18896,
    'definition': '<b>ENMAR\'BLE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To make hard as marble; to harden.',
  },
  'Enmesh': {
    'id': 18897,
    'definition': '<b>ENMESH\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [from mesh.] To net; to entangle to entrap.',
  },
  'Enmity': {
    'id': 18898,
    'definition': '<b>EN\'MITY</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. The quality of being an enemy; the opposite of friendship; ill will; hatred; unfriendly dispositions; malevolence. It expresses more than aversion and less than malice,and differs from displeasure in denoting a fixed or rooted hatred, whereas displeasure is more transient.<br><br>I will put enmity between thee and the woman. Gen 3.<br><br>The carnal mind is enmity against God.Rom 8.<br><br>2. A state of opposition.<br><br>The friendship of the world is enmity with God. James 4.',
  },
  'Enneacontahedral': {
    'id': 18899,
    'definition': '<b>ENNEACONTAHE\'DRAL</b>, <i>a.</i> Having ninety faces.',
  },
  'Enneagon': {
    'id': 18900,
    'definition': '<b>EN\'NEAGON</b>, <i>n.</i> [Gr. nine, an angle.] In geometry, a polygon or figure with nine sides or nine angles.',
  },
  'Enneander': {
    'id': 18901,
    'definition': '<b>ENNEAN\'DER</b>, <i>n.</i> [Gr. nine, a male.] In botany, a plant having nine stamens.',
  },
  'Enneandrian': {
    'id': 18902,
    'definition': '<b>ENNEAN\'DRIAN</b>, <i>a.</i> Having nine stamens.',
  },
  'Enneapetalous': {
    'id': 18903,
    'definition': '<b>ENNEAPET\'ALOUS</b>, <i>a.</i> [Gr. nine, a leaf.] Having nine petals or flower-leaves.',
  },
  'Enneatical': {
    'id': 18904,
    'definition': '<b>ENNEAT\'ICAL</b>, <i>a.</i> [Gr. nine.] Enneatical days, are every ninth day of a disease. Enneatical years, are every ninth year of a man\'s life.',
