  'Exulcerate': {
    'id': 20529,
    'definition': '<b>EXUL\'CERATE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [L. exulcero; ex and ulcero, to ulcerate, ulcus, an ulcer.]<br><br>1. To cause or produce an ulcer or ulcers.<br><br>2. To afflict; to corrode; to fret or anger.<br><br><b>EXUL\'CERATE</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To become an ulcer or ulcerous.',
  },
  'Exulcerated': {
    'id': 20530,
    'definition': '<b>EXUL\'CERATED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Affected with ulcers; having become ulcerous.',
  },
  'Exulcerating': {
    'id': 20531,
    'definition': '<b>EXUL\'CERATING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Producing ulcers on; fretting; becoming ulcerous.',
  },
  'Exulceration': {
    'id': 20532,
    'definition': '<b>EXULCERA\'TION</b>, <i>n.</i> The act of causing ulcers on a body, or the process of becoming ulcerous; the beginning erosion which wears away the substance and forms an ulcer..<br><br>1. A fretting; exacerbation; corrosion.',
