  'Faintly': {
    'id': 20678,
    'definition': '<b>FA\'INTLY</b>, <i>adv.<br><br></i> 1. In a feeble, languid manner; without vigor or activity; as, to attack or defend faintly.<br><br>2. With a feeble flame; as, a torch burns faintly.<br><br>3. With a feeble light; as, the candle burns faintly.<br><br>4. With little force; as, to breathe faintly.<br><br>5. Without force of representation; imperfectly; as, to describe faintly what we have seen.<br><br>6. In a low tone; with a feeble voice; as, to speak faintly.<br><br>7. Without spirit or courage; timorously.<br><br>He faintly now declines the fatal strife.',
