    'definition': '<b>FALCA\'DE</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. falx, a sickle or sythe.]<br><br>A horse is said to make a falcade, when he throws himself on his haunches two or three times, as in very quick curvets; that is a falcade is a bending very low.',
