    'definition': '<b>FALSELY</b>, <i>adv.</i> fols\'ly.<br><br>1. In a manner contrary to truth and fact; not truly; as, to speak or swear falsely; to testify falsely.<br><br>2. Treacherously; perfidiously.<br><br>Swear to me - that thou wilt not deal falsely with me.<br><br>Gen 21.<br><br>3. Erroneously; by mistake.',
