  'Filacer': {
    'id': 21415,
    'definition': '<b>FIL\'ACER</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>An officer in the English Court of Common Pleas, so called from filing the writs on which he makes process. There are fourteen of them in their several divisions and counties. They make out all original processes, real, personal and mixed.',
  },
  'Filament': {
    'id': 21416,
    'definition': '<b>FIL\'AMENT</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. filamenta, threads, from filum.]<br><br>A thread; a fiber. In anatomy and natural history, a fine thread of which flesh, nerves, skin, plants, roots, &c., and also some minerals, are composed. So the spider\'s web is composed of filaments. The threadlike part of the stamens of plants, is called the filament.',
  },
  'Filamentous': {
