  'Filthiness': {
    'id': 21456,
    'definition': '<b>FILTH\'INESS</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. The state of being filthy.<br><br>2. Foulness; dirtiness; filth; nastiness.<br><br>Carry forth the filthiness out of the holy place.<br><br>2 Chr 29.<br><br>3. Corruption; pollution; defilement by sin; impurity.<br><br>Let us cleanse ourselves from all filthiness of the flesh and spirit, perfecting holiness in the fear of God. 2 Cor 7.',
  },
  'Filthy': {
    'id': 21457,
    'definition': '<b>FILTH\'Y</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Dirty; foul; unclean; nasty.<br><br>2. Polluted; defiled by sinful practices; morally impure.<br><br>He that is filthy, let him be filthy still. Rev 22.<br><br>3. Obtained by base and dishonest means; as filthy lucre. Titus 1.',
