  'Flax': {
    'id': 21777,
    'definition': '<b>FLAX</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. A plant of the genus Linum, consisting of a single slender stalk, the skin or herl of which is used for making thread and cloth, called linen, cambric, lawn, lace, &c. The skin consists of fine fibers, which may be so separated as to be spun into threads as fine as silk.<br><br>2. The skin or fibrous part of the plant when broken and cleaned by hatcheling or combing.',
  },
  'Flaxcomb': {
    'id': 21778,
    'definition': '<b>FLAX\'COMB</b>, <i>n.</i> An instrument with teeth through which flax is drawn for separating from it the tow or coarser part and the shives. In America, we call it a hatchel.',
