  'Forecast': {
    'id': 22267,
    'definition': '<b>FOREC\'AST</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To foresee; to provide against.<br><br>It is wisdom to forecast consequences.<br><br>2. To scheme; to plan before execution.<br><br>He shall forecast his devices against the strong holds. Dan 11.<br><br>3. To adjust; contrive or appoint beforehand<br><br>The time so well forecast.<br><br><b>FOREC\'AST</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To form a scheme previously; to contrive beforehand.<br><br>Forecasting how his foe he might annoy.<br><br><b>FO\'REC\'AST</b>, <i>n.</i> Previous contrivance; foresight, or the antecedent determination proceeding from it; as a man of little forecast.',
  },
  'Forecaster': {
