  'Forecastle': {
    'id': 22270,
    'definition': '<b>FO\'RECASTLE</b>, <i>n.</i> A short deck in the forepart of a ship above the upper deck usually terminated in ships of war with a breast-work; the foremost part forming the top of the beak-head, and the hind part reaching to the after part of the fore chains.',
