  'Foreclose': {
    'id': 22273,
    'definition': '<b>FORECLO\'SE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> s as z. To shut up; to preclude; to stop; to prevent.<br><br>The embargo with Spain foreclosed this trade.<br><br>To foreclose a mortgager, in law, is to cut him off from his equity of redemption, or the power of redeeming the mortgaged premises, by a judgment of court.<br><br>[To foreclose a mortgage is not technically correct, but is often used.]',
