  'Foreguess': {
    'id': 22295,
    'definition': '<b>FOREGUESS\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To conjecture. [Bad.]',
  },
  'Forehand': {
    'id': 22296,
    'definition': '<b>FO\'REHAND</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. The part of a horse which is before the rider.<br><br>2. The chief part.<br><br><b>FO\'REHAND</b>, <i>a.</i> Done sooner than is regular.<br><br>And so extenuate the forehand sin.',
  },
  'Forehanded': {
    'id': 22297,
    'definition': '<b>FO\'REHANDED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Early; timely; seasonable; as a forehanded care.<br><br>2. In America, in good circumstances as to property; free from debt and possessed of property; as a forehanded farmer.<br><br>3. Formed in the foreparts.<br><br>A substantial true-bred beast, bravely forehanded.',
  },
  'Forehead': {
    'id': 22298,
    'definition': '<b>FOREHEAD</b>, <i>n.</i> for\'hed, or rather for\'ed.<br><br>1. The part of the face which extends from the hair on the top of the head to the eyes.<br><br>2. Impudence; confidence; assurance; audaciousness.',
