  'Girt': {
    'id': 23849,
    'definition': '<b>GIRT</b>, <i>pret.</i> and pp. of gird.<br><br><b>GIRT</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To gird; to surround.<br><br>[This verb, if derived from the noun, girt, may be proper.]<br><br><b>GIRT',
  },
  'Girth': {
    'id': 23850,
    'definition': '<b>GIRTH</b>, <i>n.</i> The band or strap by which a saddle or any burden on a horse\'s back is made fast, by passing under his belly.<br><br>1. A circular bandage.<br><br>2. The compass measured by a firth or inclosing bandage.<br><br>He\'s a lusty, jolly fellow, that lives well, at least three yards in the girth.<br><br><b>GIRTH</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To bind with a girth.',
