  'Glare': {
    'id': 23908,
    'definition': '<b>GLARE</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. A bright dazzling light; clear, brilliant luster or splendor, that dazzles the eyes.<br><br>The frame of burnished steel that cast a glare.<br><br>2. A fierce, piercing look.<br><br>--About them round,<br><br>A lion now he stalks with fiery glare.<br><br>3. A viscous transparent substance. [See <a href="dict://Glair">Glair</a>.]<br><br><b>GLARE</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To shine with a clear, bright, dazzling light; as glaring light.<br><br>The cavern glares with new admitted light.<br><br>1. To look with fierce, piercing eyes.<br><br>They glared, like angry lions.<br><br>2. To shine with excessive luster; to be ostentatiously splendid; as a glaring dress.<br><br>She glares in balls, front boxes and the ring.<br><br><b>GLARE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To shoot a dazzling light.',
