  'Groundly': {
    'id': 24722,
    'definition': '<b>GROUND\'LY</b>, <i>adv.</i> Upon principles; solidly. [A bad word and not used.]<br><br><b>GROUND\'-NUT</b>, <i>n.</i> A plant, the Arachis, a native of South America.<br><br><b>GROUND\'-OAK</b>, <i>n.</i> A sapling of oak.<br><br><b>GROUND\'-PINE</b>,n. A plant, a species of Teucrium or germander; said to be so called from its resinous smell.<br><br><b>GROUND\'-PLATE</b>, <i>n.</i> In architecture,the ground-plates are the outermost pieces of timber lying on or near the ground, framed into one another with mortises and tenons.',
