  'Hawse': {
    'id': 25448,
    'definition': '<b>HAWSE</b>, <i>n.</i> hawz. [See <a href="dict://Halser">Halser</a>.] The situation of a ship moored with two anchors from the bows, one on the starboard, the other on the larboard bow; as, the ship has a clear hawse, or a foul hawse. A foul hawse is when the cables cross each other or are twisted together.',
