  'Hectic': {
    'id': 25683,
    'definition': '<b>HEC\'TIC<br><br>HEC\'TICAL</b>, <i>a.</i> [Gr. habit of body, to have.] Habitual; denoting a slow, continual fever, marked by preternatural, though remitting heat, which precedes and accompanies the consumption or phthisis; as a hectic fever.<br><br>1. Affected with hectic fevers; as a hectic patient.<br><br>2. Troubled with a morbid heat.<br><br>No hectic student scares the gentle maid.<br><br><b>HEC\'TIC</b>, <i>n.</i> A hectic; or habitual fever.',
  },
