  'Helm': {
    'id': 25776,
    'definition': '<b>HELM</b>, <i>a</i> termination, denotes defense; as in Sighelm, victorious defense. [See <a href="dict://Helmet">Helmet</a>.]<br><br><b>HELM</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. The instrument by which a ship is steered, consisting of a rudder, a tiller, and in large vessels, a wheel. [See <a href="dict://Rudder">Rudder</a>.]<br><br>2. Station of government; the place of direction or management; as, to be at the helm in the administration.<br><br><b>HELM</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To steer; to guide; to direct. [Little used.]<br><br>1. To cover with a helmet.<br><br><b>HELM',
  },
  'Helmed': {
    'id': 25777,
    'definition': '<b>HELM\'ED<br><br>HELM\'ET</b>, <i>n.</i> Defensive armor for the head; a head-piece; a morion. The helmet is worn by horsemen to defend the head against the broad sword.<br><br>1. The part of a coat of arms that bears the crest.<br><br>2. The upper part of a retort.<br><br>3. In botany, the upper lip of a ringent corol.',
