  'High-Place': {
    'id': 26113,
    'definition': '<b>HIGH-PLACE</b>, <i>n.</i> In Scripture, an eminence or mound on which sacrifices were offered. Before the temple was built in Jerusalem, sacrifices were offered to Jehovah by his worshipers, on high places; but afterwards such mounds were devoted to idolatrous sacrifices.',
