    'definition': '<b>HOL\'LOW-ROOT</b>, <i>n.</i> A plant, tuberous moschatel, or inglorious, constituting the genus Adoxa; a low plant, whose leaves and flowers smell like musk; hence it is sometimes called musk-crowfoot.',
