  'Lazily': {
    'id': 31540,
    'definition': '<b>LA\'ZILY</b>, <i>adv.</i> [from lazy.] In a heavy, sluggish manner; sluggishly.<br><br>Whether he lazily and listlessly dreams away his time.',
  },
  'Laziness': {
    'id': 31541,
    'definition': '<b>LA\'ZINESS</b>, <i>n.</i> [from lazy.]<br><br>1. The state or quality of being lazy; indisposition to action or exertion; indolence; sluggishness; heaviness in motion; habitual sloth. Laziness differs from idleness; the latter being a mere defect or cessation of action, but laziness is sloth, with natural or habitual disinclination to action.<br><br>Laziness travels so slowly, that poverty soon overtakes him.<br><br>2. Slowness; tardiness.',
