  'Lazulite': {
    'id': 31544,
    'definition': '<b>LAZ\'ULITE</b>, <i>n.</i> A mineral of a light, indigo blue color, occurring in small masses, or crystallized in oblique four-sided prisms.',
  },
  'Lazy': {
    'id': 31545,
    'definition': '<b>LA\'ZY</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. laxus, and it is doubtful whether this is of the same family.]<br><br>1. Disinclined to action or exertion; naturally or habitually slothful; sluggish; indolent; averse to labor; heavy in motion.<br><br>Wicked men will ever live like rogues, and not fall to work, but be lazy and spend victuals.<br><br>2. Slow; moving slowly or apparently with labor; as a lazy stream.<br><br>The night-owl\'s lazy flight.',
