  'Lea': {
    'id': 31547,
    'definition': '<b>LEA,<br><br>LEACH</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [See <a href="dict://leak">leak</a>. Perhaps L. lix may be from the same root.]<br><br>To wash, as ashes, by percolation, or causing water to pass through them, and thus to separate from them the alkali. The water thus charged with alkali, is called lye.<br><br><b>LEACH</b>, <i>n.</i> A quantity of wood ashes, through which water passes, and thus imbibes the alkali.',
