    'definition': '<b>LE\'ADER</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. One that leads or conducts; a guide; a conductor.<br><br>2. A chief; a commander; a captain.<br><br>3. One who goes first.<br><br>4. The chief of a party or faction; as the leader of the whigs or of the tories; a leader of the Jacobins.<br><br>5. a performer who leads a band or choir in music.',
