  'Lieutenant': {
    'id': 31922,
    'definition': '<b>LIEUTENANT</b>, <i>n.</i> luten\'ant. [L. tenens, holding.]<br><br>1. An officer who supplies the place of a superior in his absence. Officers of this kind are civil, as the lord-lieutenant of a kingdom or county; or military, as a lieutenant general, a lieutenant colonel.<br><br>2. In military affairs, the second commissioned officer in a company of infantry cavalry or artillery.<br><br>3. In ships of war, the officer next in rank to the captain.',
