    'definition': '<b>LOOP\'HOLE</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. A small aperture in the bulk-head and other parts of a merchant ship, through which small arms are fired at an enemy.<br><br>2. A hole or aperture that gives a passage.<br><br>3. A passage for escape; means of escape.',
