  'Lop': {
    'id': 32431,
    'definition': '<b>LOP</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [Eng. flap. The primary sense is evidently to fall or fell, or to strike down, and I think it connected with flap.]<br><br>1. To cut off, as the top or extreme part of any thing; to shorten by cutting off the extremities; as, to lop a tree or its branches.<br><br>With branches lopp\'d in wood, or mountain fell\'d.<br><br>2. To cut off, as exuberances; to separate, as superfluous parts.<br><br>Expunge the whole, or lop the excrescent parts.<br><br>3. to cut partly off and bend down; as, to lop the trees or saplings of a hedge.<br><br>4. To let fall; to flap; as, a horse lops his ears.<br><br><b>LOP</b>, <i>n.</i> that which is cut from trees.<br><br>Else both body and lop will be of little value.<br><br><b>LOP</b>, <i>n.</i> a flea. [Local.]',
  },
