  'May-Dew': {
    'id': 33577,
    'definition': '<b>MA\'Y-DEW</b>, <i>n.</i> The dew of May, which is said to whiten linen, and to afford by repeated distillations, a red and odoriferous spirit. It has been supposed that from the preparation of this dew, the Rosicrucians took their name.',
