  'Misprise': {
    'id': 34549,
    'definition': '<b>MISPRI\'SE<br><br>MISPRISION</b>, <i>n.</i> misprizh\'un. [supra.] Neglect; contempt.<br><br>1. In law, any high offense under the degree of capital, but nearly bordering thereon. Misprision is contained in every treason and felony. Misprisions are divided into negative and positive; negative, which consist in the concealment of something which ought to be revealed; and positive, which consist in the commission of something which ought not to be done. Misprision of treason, consists in a bare knowledge and concealment of treason, without assenting to it.<br><br>Maladministration in offices of high public trust, is a positive misprision.<br><br>1. Mistake; oversight; contempt. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Misprize': {
    'id': 34550,
    'definition': '<b>MISPRI\'ZE</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To mistake.<br><br>2. To slight or undervalue.<br><br>O for those vanish\'d hours, so much mispris\'d.',
  },
