    'definition': '<b>MOAT</b>, <i>n.</i> In fortification, a ditch or deep trench round the rampart of a castle or other fortified place. It is sometimes filled with water.<br><br><b>MOAT</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To surround with a ditch for defense; as a moated castle.',
  },
  'Mob': {
    'id': 34731,
    'definition': '<b>MOB</b>, <i>n.</i> [from L. mobilis, movable, variable.]<br><br>1. A crowd or promiscuous multitude of people, rude, tumultuous and disorderly.<br><br>2. A disorderly assembly.<br><br>Had every Athenian citizen been a Socrates, every Athenian assembly would still have been a mob.<br><br>3. A huddled dress.<br><br><b>MOB</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To attack in a disorderly crowd; to harass tumultuously.<br><br>1. To wrap up in a cowl or vail.',
  },
  'Mobbish': {
    'id': 34732,
    'definition': '<b>MOB\'BISH</b>, <i>a.</i> Like a mob; tumultuous; mean; vulgar.',
