  'Nautilus': {
    'id': 35723,
    'definition': '<b>NAUTILUS</b>, <i>n.</i> [L.,Gr. A ship] A genus of marine animals, whose shell consists of one spiral valve divided into several apartments by partitions. There are many species. This animal, when it sails, extends two of its arms, and between these supports a membrane that serves as a sail. With two other arms it rows or steers.<br><br>Learn of the little nautilus to sail.',
