  'Neophyte': {
    'id': 35893,
    'definition': '<b>NEOPHYTE</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. A new convert or proselyte; a name given by the early Christians to such heathens as had recently embraced the Christian faith, and were considered as regenerated by baptism.<br><br>2. A novice; one newly admitted to the order of priest.<br><br>3. A tyro; a beginner in learning.',
