  'Officiate': {
    'id': 36900,
    'definition': '<b>OFFI\'CIATE</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To act as an officer in his office; to transact the appropriate business of an office or public trust. At this court the chief justice officiated.<br><br>The bishops and priests officiate at the altar.<br><br>2. To perform the appropriate official duties of another.<br><br><b>OFFI\'CIATE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To give in consequence of office.<br><br>The stars officiate light. [Improper.]',
