    'definition': '<b>OFFI\'CIOUSLY</b>, <i>adv.<br><br></i> 1. Kindly; with solicitous care.<br><br>Let thy goats officiously be nurs\'d.<br><br>2. With importunate or excessive forwardness.<br><br>Flattering crowds officiously appear, to give themselves, not you, a happy year.<br><br>3. In a busy meddling manner.',
