    'definition': '<b>OFFI\'CIOUSNESS</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. Eagerness to serve; usually, an excess of zeal to serve others, or improper forwardness, interposing in affairs without being desired, or with a disposition to meddle with the concerns of others.<br><br>2. Service. [Little used.]',
