  'Opiate': {
    'id': 37116,
    'definition': '<b>O\'PIATE</b>, <i>n.</i> [from opium.]<br><br>1. Primarily, a medicine of a thicker consistence than syrup, prepared with opium.<br><br>A soft electuary.<br><br>Electuaries when soft are call opiata.<br><br>But in modern usage generally,<br><br>2. Any medicine that has the quality of inducing sleep or repose; a narcotic.<br><br>3. That which induces rest or inaction; that which quiets uneasiness.<br><br>They chose atheism as an opiate.<br><br><b>O\'PIATE</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Inducing sleep; soporiferous; somniferous; narcotic.<br><br>2. Causing rest or inaction.',
