    'definition': '<b>OUTL\'AST</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To last longer than something else; to exceed in duration. Candles laid in bran will outlast others of the same stuff.',
  },
  'Outlaw': {
    'id': 37547,
    'definition': '<b>OUT\'LAW</b>, <i>n.</i> A person excluded from the benefit of the law, or deprived of its protection. Formerly any person might kill an outlaw; but it is now held unlawful for any person to put to death an outlaw, except the sheriff, who has a warrant for that purpose.<br><br><b>OUT\'LAW</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To deprive of the benefit and protection of law; to proscribe.',
  },
  'Outlawed': {
    'id': 37548,
    'definition': '<b>OUT\'LAWED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Excluded from the benefit of law.',
  },
  'Outlawing': {
