    'definition': '<b>PEAT-MOSS</b>, <i>n.</i> [peat and moss.] An earthy material used as fuel.<br><br>1. A fen producing peat.',
  },
  'Pebble': {
    'id': 38791,
    'definition': '<b>PEB\'BLE<br><br>PEB\'BLE-CRYSTAL</b>, <i>n.</i> A crystal in form of nodules, found in earthy stratums and irregular in shape.',
  },
  'Pebbled': {
    'id': 38792,
    'definition': '<b>PEB\'BLED</b>, <i>a.</i> Abounding with pebbles.',
  },
  'Pebblestone': {
    'id': 38793,
    'definition': '<b>PEB\'BLESTONE</b>, <i>n.</i> In popular usage, a roundish stone of any kind from the size of a nut to that of a man\'s head. In a philosophical sense, minerals distinguished from flints by their variety of colors, consisting of crystalline matter debased by earths of various kinds, with veins, clouds and other variegations, formed by incrustation round a central nucleus, but sometimes the effect of a simple concretion. Pebbles are much used in the pavement of streets.<br><br>A general term for water-worn minerals.',
  },
  'Pebbly': {
    'id': 38794,
    'definition': '<b>PEB\'BLY</b>, <i>a.</i> Full of pebbles; abounding with small roundish stones.',
  },
  'Pec-Cary': {
    'id': 38795,
    'definition': '<b>PEC-CARY</b>, <i>n.</i> A quadruped of Mexico, in general appearance resembling a hog, but its body is less bulky, its legs shorter, and its bristles thicker and stronger, like the quills of the porcupine. Its color is black and white, and it has on the hind part of the back a protuberance like the navel of other animals, with an orifice form which issues a liquor of a very strong scent.',
  },
  'Pecary': {
    'id': 38796,
    'definition': '<b>PEC\'ARY<br><br>PECCABIL\'ITY</b>, <i>n.</i> [from peccable.] State of being subject to sin; capacity of sinning.',
