    'definition': '<b>PIR\'RY</b>, <i>n.</i> A rough gale of wind; a storm. [Not used.]',
  },
  'Piscary': {
    'id': 39891,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'CARY</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. piscis, a fish; piscor, to fish.]<br><br>In law, the right or privilege of fishing in another man\'s waters.',
  },
  'Piscation': {
    'id': 39892,
    'definition': '<b>PISCA\'TION</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. piscatio. See <a href="dict://Piscary">Piscary</a> and Fish.]<br><br>The act or practice of fishing.',
  },
  'Piscatory': {
    'id': 39893,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'CATORY</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. piscatorius.] Relating to fishes or to fishing; as a piscatory eclogue.',
  },
  'Pisces': {
    'id': 39894,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'CES</b>, <i>n.</i> plu. [L. piscis.] In astronomy, the Fishes, the twelfth sign or constellation in the zodiac.',
  },
  'Piscine': {
    'id': 39895,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'CINE</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. piscis, a fish.]<br><br>Pertaining to fish or fishes; as piscine remains.',
  },
  'Piscivorous': {
    'id': 39896,
    'definition': '<b>PISCIV\'OROUS</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. piscis, a fish,and voro, to eat.]<br><br>Feeding or subsisting on fishes. Many species of aquatic fowls are piscivorous.',
  },
  'Pish': {
    'id': 39897,
    'definition': '<b>PISH</b>, <i>exclam.</i> A word expressing contempt; sometimes spoken and written pshaw.<br><br><b>PISH</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To express contempt.',
  },
  'Pisiform': {
    'id': 39898,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'IFORM</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. pisum, a pea, and forma, form.]<br><br>Having the form of a pea.<br><br>Masses of pisiform argillaceous iron ore.',
  },
  'Pismire': {
    'id': 39899,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'MIRE</b>, <i>n.</i> The insect called the ant or emmet.',
  },
  'Pisolite': {
    'id': 39900,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'OLITE</b>, <i>n.</i> [Gr. a pea, and a stone.] Peastone, a carbonate of lime, slightly colored by the oxyd of iron. It occurs in little globular concretions of the size of a pea or larger, which usually contain each a grain of sand as a nucleus. These concretions in union sometimes compose entire beds of secondary mountains. It is sometimes called calcarious tufa.',
  },
  'Pisophalt': {
    'id': 39901,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'OPHALT</b>, <i>n.</i> Pea-mineral or mineral-pea; a soft bitumen, black and of a strong pungent smell. It appears to be petrol passing to asphalt. It holds a middle place between petrol, which is liquid,and asphalt, which is dry and brittle.',
  },
  'Piss': {
    'id': 39902,
    'definition': '<b>PISS</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To discharge the liquor secreted by the kidneys and lodged in the urinary bladder.<br><br><b>PISS</b>, <i>n.</i> Urine; the liquor secreted by the kidneys into the bladder of an animal and discharged through the proper channel.',
  },
  'Pissabed': {
    'id': 39903,
    'definition': '<b>PISS\'ABED</b>, <i>n.</i> The vulgar name of a yellow flower, growing among grass.',
  },
  'Pissasphalt': {
    'id': 39904,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'SASPHALT</b>, <i>n.</i> [Gr. pitch, and asphalt.] Earth-pitch; pitch mixed with bitumen, natural or artificial; a fluid opake mineral substance, thick and inflammable,but leaving a residuum after burning.',
  },
  'Pissburnt': {
    'id': 39905,
    'definition': '<b>PISS\'BURNT</b>, <i>a.</i> Stained with urine.',
  },
  'Pist': {
    'id': 39906,
    'definition': '<b>PIST<br><br>PISTA\'CHIO</b>,n. [L. pistachia.] The nut of the Pistacia terebinthus or turpentine tree, containing a kernel of a pale greenish color, of a pleasant taste, resembling that of the almond, and yielding a well tasted oil. It is wholesome and nutritive. The tree grows in Syria, Arabia and Persia.',
  },
  'Pistacite': {
    'id': 39907,
    'definition': '<b>PIS\'TACITE<br><br>PISTAREE\'N</b>, <i>n.</i> A silver coin of the value of 17 or 18 cents, or 9d sterling.',
