  },
  'Pontif': {
    'id': 40550,
    'definition': '<b>PONT\'IF</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. pontifex; said to be from pons, a bridge, and facio, to make.] A high priest. The Romans had a college of pontifs; the Jews had their pontifs; and in modern times, the pope is called pontif or sovereign pontif.',
