  'Primer-Seizin': {
    'id': 41527,
    'definition': '<b>PRIMER-SE\'IZIN</b>, <i>n.</i> [prime and seizin.] In feudal law, the right of the king, when a tenant in capite died seized of a knight\'s fee, to receive of the heir, if of full age, one year\'s profits of the land if in possession, and half a year\'s profits if the land was in reversions expectant on an estate for life; abolished by 12 Car.2.',
