  'Primitive': {
    'id': 41537,
    'definition': '<b>PRIM\'ITIVE</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. primitivus; from primus, first.]<br><br>1. Pertaining to the beginning or origin; original; first; as the primitive state of Adam; primitive innocence; primitive ages; the primitive church; the primitive christian church or institutions; the primitive fathers.<br><br>2. Formal; affectedly solemn; imitating the supposed gravity of old times.<br><br>3. Original; primary; radical; not derived; as a primitive verb in grammar.<br><br>Primitive rocks, in geology, rocks supposed to be first formed, being irregularly crystallized, and aggregated without a cement,<br><br>and containing no organic remains; as granite, gneiss, &c.<br><br><b>PRIM\'ITIVE</b>, <i>n.</i> An original word; a word not derived from another.',
  },
  'Primitively': {
    'id': 41538,
