  'Pusillanimity': {
    'id': 42554,
    'definition': '<b>PUSILLANIM\'ITY</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. pusillanimitas; pusillus,small, weak, and animus,courage.] Want of that firmness and strength of mind which constitutes courage or fortitude; weakness of spirit; cowardliness; that feebleness of mind which shrinks from trifling or imaginary dangers.<br><br>It is obvious to distinguish between an act of pusillanimity and an act of great modesty or humility.',
  },
  'Pusillanimous': {
    'id': 42555,
    'definition': '<b>PUSILLAN\'IMOUS</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Destitute of that strength and firmness of mind which constitute courage, bravery and fortitude; being of weak courage; mean spirited; cowardly; applied to persons; as a pusillanimous prince.<br><br>2. Proceeding from weakness of mind or want of courage; feeble; as pusillanimous counsels.',
