  'Putrefy': {
    'id': 42576,
    'definition': '<b>PU\'TREFY</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [L. putrefacio; putris,putrid, and facio, to make.]<br><br>1. To cause to dissolve; to disorganize and reduce to the simple constituent elements, as animal or vegetable bodies; to cause to rot. Heat and moisture soon putrefy dead flesh or vegetables.<br><br>2. To corrupt; to make foul; as, to putrefy the air. [Little used.]<br><br>3. To make morbid, carious or gangrenous; as, to putrefy an ulcer or wound.<br><br><b>PU\'TREFY</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To dissolve and return to the original distinct elements, as animal and vegetable substances deprived of the living principle; to rot.',
