  'Quell': {
    'id': 42840,
    'definition': '<b>QUELL</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To crush; to subdue; to cause to cease; as, to quell an insurrection or sedition.<br><br>2. To quiet; to allay; to reduce to peace; as, to quell the tumult of the soul.<br><br>3. To subdue; to reduce.<br><br>This quell\'d her pride.<br><br><b>QUELL</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To die; to abate.<br><br><b>QUELL</b>, <i>n.</i> Murder. [Not in use.]',
