  'Rejoice': {
    'id': 44362,
    'definition': '<b>REJOICE</b>, <i>v.i.</i> rejois\'.<br><br>To experience joy and gladness in a high degree; to be exhilarated with lively and pleasurable sensations; to exult.<br><br>When the righteous are in authority, the people rejoice; but when the wicked beareth rule, the people mourn. Prov 29.<br><br>I will rejoice in thy salvation. Psa 9.<br><br><b>REJOICE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> rejois\'. To make joyful; to gladden; to animate with lively pleasurable sensations; to exhilarate.<br><br>Whoso loveth wisdom rejoiceth his father. Prov 29.<br><br>While she, great saint, rejoices heaven.',
  },
  'Rejoiced': {
    'id': 44363,
    'definition': '<b>REJOIC\'ED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Made glad; exhilarated.',
  },
  'Rejoicer': {
    'id': 44364,
    'definition': '<b>REJOIC\'ER</b>, <i>n.</i> One that rejoices.',
  },
  'Rejoicing': {
    'id': 44365,
    'definition': '<b>REJOIC\'ING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Animating with gladness; exhilarating; feeling joy.<br><br><b>REJOIC\'ING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Animating with gladness; exhilarating; feeling joy.<br><br><b>REJOIC\'ING</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. The act of expressing joy and gladness.<br><br>The voice of rejoicing and salvation is in the tabernacles of the righteous. Psa 118.<br><br>2. The subject of joy.<br><br>Thy testimonies have I taken as an heritage forever, for they are the rejoicing of my heart. Psa 119.<br><br>3. The experience of joy. Gal 6.',
  },
  'Rejoicingly': {
    'id': 44366,
    'definition': '<b>REJOIC\'INGLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> With joy or exultation.',
  },
  'Rejoin': {
    'id': 44367,
    'definition': '<b>REJOIN\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [re and join.]<br><br>1. To join again; to unite after separation.<br><br>2. To meet one again.<br><b>REJOIN\'</b>, <i>v.i.<br><br></i> 1. To answer to a reply.<br><br>2. In law pleadings, to answer, as the defendant to the plantif\'s replication.',
  },
  'Rejoinder': {
    'id': 44368,
    'definition': '<b>REJOIND\'ER</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. An answer to a reply; or in general, an answer.<br><br>2. In law pleadings, the defendants\'s answer to the plantif\'s replication.',
  },
  'Rejoined': {
