  'Rosary': {
    'id': 45848,
    'definition': '<b>RO\'SARY</b>, <i>n.</i> s as z. [L. rosarium. See <a href="dict://Rose">Rose</a>.]<br><br>1. A bed of roses, or place where roses grow.<br><br>2. A chaplet.<br><br>3. A string of beads used by Roman catholics, on which they count their prayers.',
  },
  'Rosasic': {
    'id': 45849,
    'definition': '<b>ROSAS\'IC</b>, <i>a.</i> The rosasic acid is obtained from the urine of persons affected with intermitting and nervous fevers.',
  },
  'Roscid': {
    'id': 45850,
    'definition': '<b>ROS\'CID</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. roscidus, from ros, dew.]<br><br>Dewy; containing dew, or consisting of dew. [Not used.]',
  },
  'Rose': {
    'id': 45851,
    'definition': '<b>ROSE</b>, <i>n.</i> s as z. [L., Gr. from the root of red, ruddy. See <a href="dict://Red">Red</a>.]<br><br>1. A plant and flower of the genus Rosa, of many species and varieties, as the wild canine or dog-rose, the white rose, the red rose, the cinnamon rose, the eglantine or sweet briar, &c. There are five petals; the calyx is urceolate, quinquefid, and corneous; the seeds are numerous, hispid, and fixed to the inside of the calyx.<br><br>2. A knot of ribbon in the form of a rose, used as an ornamental tie of a shoe.<br><br>Under the rose, in secret; privately; in a manner that forbids disclosure.<br><br>Rose of Jericho, a plant growing on the plain of Jericho, the Anastatica hierochuntica.<br><br><b>ROSE</b>, <i>pret.</i> of rise.',
  },
