  'Rupture': {
    'id': 46103,
    'definition': '<b>RUP\'TURE</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. ruptus, rumpo, to break.]<br><br>1. The act of breaking or bursting; the state of being broken or violently parted; as the rupture of the skin; the rupture of a vessel or fiber.<br><br>2. Hernia; a preternatural protrusion of the contents of the abdomen.<br><br>3. Breach of peace or concord, either between individuals or nations; between nations, open hostility or war. We say, the parties or nations have come to an open rupture.<br><br>He knew that policy would disincline Napoleon from a rupture with his family.<br><br><b>RUP\'TURE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To break; to burst; to part by violence; as, to rupture a blood vessel.<br><br><b>RUP\'TURE</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To suffer a breach of disruption.',
  },
  'Rupture-Wort': {
