    'definition': '<b>SCA\'LY</b>, <i>a.</i> [from scale.]<br><br>1. Covered or abounding with scales; rough; as a scaly fish; the scaly crocodile.<br><br>2. Resembling scales, lamina or layers.<br><br>3. In botany, composed of scales lying over each other, as a scaly bulb; having scales scattered over it, as a scaly stem.',
