    'id': 47261,
    'definition': '<b>SE\'ALER</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. One who seals; an officer in chancery who seals writs and instruments.<br><br>2. In New England, <i>an</i> officer appointed by the town or other proper authority, to examine and try weithts and measures, and set a stamp on such as are according to the standards established by the state; also, an officer who inspects lether and stamps such as is good. These are called sealers of weights and measures, and sealers of lethers.',
