    'definition': '<b>SEARCE</b>, <i>v.</i> t. sers. To shift; to bolt; to separate the fine part of meal from the coarse. [Little used.]<br><br><b>SEARCE</b>, <i>n.</i> sers. A sieve; a bolter. [Little used.]',
