    'definition': '<b>SHIRL</b>, <i>a</i> different spelling of shorl. [See <a href="dict://Shorl">Shorl</a>.]',
  },
  'Shirley': {
    'id': 48273,
    'definition': '<b>SHIR\'LEY</b>, <i>n.</i> A bird, by some called the greater bullfinch; having the upper part of the body a dark brown, and the throat and breast read.',
  },
  'Shirt': {
    'id': 48274,
    'definition': '<b>SHIRT</b>, <i>n.</i> shurt. [L. curtus.] A loose garment of linen, cotton or other material, worn by men and boys next the body.<br><br>It is folly for a nation to export beef and linen, while a great part of the peaple are obliged to subsist on potatoes, and have no shirts to wear. A.M.<br><br><b>SHIRT</b>, <i>v.t.</i> shurt.<br><br>1. To cover or clothe, as with a shirt.<br><br>2. To change the shirt and put on a clean one.',
