  'Shrewishness': {
    'id': 48405,
    'definition': '<b>SHREW\'ISHNESS</b>, <i>n.</i> The qualities of a shrew; forwardness; petulance; turbulent clamorousness.<br><br>I have no gift in shrewishness. Shak.',
  },
  'Shriek': {
    'id': 48406,
    'definition': '<b>SHRIEK</b>, <i>v.i.</i> [L. ruga, <i>wrinkled,</i> rugo, <i>to</i> bray.] To utter a sharp shrill cry; to scream; as in sudden fright, in horror or anguish.<br><br>At this she shriek\'d aloud. Dryden.<br><br>It was the owl that shriek\'d. Shak.<br><br><b>SHRIEK</b>, <i>n.</i> A sharp shrill outcry or scream, such as is produced by sudden anger or extreme anguish.<br><br>Shrieks, <i>clamors,</i> murmurs fill the frighted town. Dryden.',
