  'Shrove-Tide': {
    'id': 48435,
    'definition': '<b>SHRO\'VE-TIDE</b>, <i>n.</i> [from shrove, <i>pret.</i> of shrive, <i>to</i> take a confession. See <a href="dict://Tide">Tide</a> and',
  },
  'Shrove-Tuesday': {
    'id': 48436,
    'definition': '<b>SHROVE-TUESDAY</b>, <i>Tuesday.]</i> Confession-time; confession-Teusday; the Tuesday after Quinquagesima Sunday; or the day immediately preceding the first of Lent, or Ash Wednesday; on which day, all the people of England when of the Catholic religion, were obliged to confess their sins one by one to their parish priests; after which they dined on pancakes or fritters. The latter ppractice still continues. The bell rung on this day is called pancake-bell.',
  },
  'Shroving': {
    'id': 48437,
    'definition': '<b>SHRO\'VING</b>, <i>n.</i> The festivity of Shrove-tide.',
  },
  'Shrub': {
    'id': 48438,
    'definition': '<b>SHRUB</b>, <i>n.</i> A low dwarf tree; a woody plant of a size less than a tree; or more strictly, a plant with several permanent woody stems, dividing from the bottom, more slender and lower than trees.<br><br>Gooseberries and currants are shrubs; oaks and cherries are trees. Locke.<br><br><b>SHRUB</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. sorbeo.] A liquor composed of acid and sugar, with spirir to preserve it; usually the acid of lemons.<br><br><b>SHRUB</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To clear of shrubs.',
  },
  'Shrubbery': {
    'id': 48439,
    'definition': '<b>SHRUB\'BERY</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. Shrubs in general.<br><br>2. A plantation of shrubs.',
  },
  'Shrubby': {
    'id': 48440,
    'definition': '<b>SHRUB\'BY</b>, <i>a.</i><br><br>1. Full of shrubs; as a shrubby plain.<br><br>2. Resembling a shrub; as plants shrubby and curled.<br><br>3. Consisting of shrubs or brush; as shrubby browze.<br><br>4. A shrubby plant is perennial, with several woody stems.',
  },
  'Shruff': {
    'id': 48441,
    'definition': '<b>SHRUFF</b>, <i>n.</i> Dross; recrement of metals. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Shrug': {
    'id': 48442,
    'definition': '<b>SHRUG</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To raise or draw up the shoulders, as in expressing horror or dissatisfaction.<br><br>They grin, they shrug,<br><br>They bow, they snarl, they scratch, they hug. Swift.<br><br><b>SHRUG</b>, <i>n.</i> A drawing up of the shoulders; a motion usually expressing dislike.<br><br>The Spaniards talk in dialogues<br><br>Of heads and shoulders, nods and shrugs. Hudibras.',
  },
  'Shrugging': {
    'id': 48443,
    'definition': '<b>SHRUG\'GING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Drawing up, as the shoulders.',
  },
  'Shrunk': {
    'id': 48444,
    'definition': '<b>SHRUNK</b>, <i>pret.</i> and pp. of shrink.',
