    'definition': '<b>SI\'LEX, SIL\'CIA</b>, <i>n.</i> One of the supposed primitive earths m usually found in the state of stone. When pure, it is perfectly white or colorless. The purer sorts are mountain crystal and quartz. Recent experiments prove this to be a compound substance, the base of which is a metal called silicium. Silica then is an oxyd of silicium.',
  },
  'Silicicalcarious': {
