  'Slily': {
    'id': 49010,
    'definition': '<b>SLILY</b>, <i>adv.</i> [from sly.] With artful or dexterous secrecy. Satan slily robs us of our grand treasure.',
  },
  'Slim': {
    'id': 49011,
    'definition': '<b>SLIM</b>, <i>a.</i> [Ice.]<br><br>1. Slender; of small diameter or thickness in proportion to the highth; as a slim person; a slim tree.<br><br>2. Weak; slight; unsubstantial.<br><br>3. Worthless.',
  },
  'Slime': {
    'id': 49012,
    'definition': '<b>SLIME</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. limus.] Soft moist earth having an adhesive quality; viscous mud. The had brick for stone, and slime had they for mortar. Gen 11.',
