  'Sneer': {
    'id': 49266,
    'definition': '<br>SNEER, v.i. [from the root of L. naris, nose; to turn up the nose.]<br><br>1. To show contempt by turning up the nose, or by a particular cast or countenance; "naso suspendere adunco."<br><br>2. To insinuate contempt by covert expression. I could be content to be a little sneered at.<br><br>3. To utter with grimace.<br><br>4. To show mirth awkwardly.<br><br><b>SNEER</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. A look of contempt, or a turning up of the nose to manifest contempt; a look of disdain, derision or ridicule.<br><br>2. An expression of ludicrous scorn.',
  },
