    'definition': '<b>SOOSHONG\', SOUCHONG\'</b>, <i>n.</i> A kind of black tea.',
  },
  'Soosoo': {
    'id': 49557,
    'definition': '<b>SOO\'SOO</b>, <i>n.</i> Among the Bengalese, the mane of a cetaceous fish, the Delphinus Gangeticus.',
  },
  'Soot': {
    'id': 49558,
    'definition': '<b>SOOT</b>, <i>n.</i> A black substance formed by combustion, or disengaged from fuel in the process of combustion, rising in fine particles and adhering to the sides of the chimney or pipe conveying the smoke. Soot consists of oil, carbon and other substances. The soot of burnt pine forms lampblack.<br><br><b>SOOT</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To cover or foul with soot.',
  },
  'Sooted': {
    'id': 49559,
    'definition': '<b>SOOT\'ED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Covered or soiled with soot.',
  },
  'Sooterkin': {
    'id': 49560,
    'definition': '<b>SOOT\'ERKIN</b>, <i>n.</i> A kind of false birth fabled to be produced by the Dutch women from sitting over their stoves.',
  },
  'Sooth': {
    'id': 49561,
    'definition': '<b>SOOTH</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. Truth; reality.<br><br>2. Prognostication.<br><br>3. Sweetness; kindness.<br><br><b>SOOTH</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Pleasing; delightful.<br><br>2. True; faithful.',
  },
  'Soothe': {
    'id': 49562,
    'definition': '<b>SOOTHE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [The sense of setting, allaying of softening, would give that of truth, and of sweet, that is, smooth.]<br><br>1. To flatter; to please with blandishments or soft words. Can I soothe tyranny? I\'ve tried the force of every reason on him. Sooth\'d and caress\'d, been angry, sooth\'d again<br><br>2. To soften; to assuage; to mollify; to calm; as, to soothe one in pain or passion; or to soothe pain. It is applied both to persons and things.<br><br>3. To gratify; to please. Sooth\'d with his future fame.',
  },
  'Soothed': {
    'id': 49563,
    'definition': '<b>SOOTH\'ED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Flattered; softened; calmed; pleased.',
  },
  'Soother': {
    'id': 49564,
    'definition': '<b>SOOTH\'ER</b>, <i>n.</i> A flatterer; he or that which softens or assuages.',
  },
  'Soothing': {
