  'Sperm': {
    'id': 49921,
    'definition': '<b>SPERM</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. sperma.]<br><br>1. Animal seed; that by which the species is propagated.<br><br>2. The head matter of a certain species of whale, called cachalot. It is called by the French blanc de baleine, the white of whales. It is found also in other parts of the body; but it is improperly named, not being a spermatic substance. Of this matter are mad candles of a beautiful white color.<br><br>3. Spawn of fishes or frogs.<br><br><b>SPERMACE"TO</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. sperma, sperm, and cetus, a whale. It is pronounced as it is written.] The same as sperm.',
