    'definition': '<b>SPRUCE</b>, <i>a.</i> Nice; trim; neat without elegance or dignity; formerly applied to things with a serious meaning; now applied to persons only.<br><br>He is so spruce, that he never can be genteel.<br><br><b>SPRUCE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To trim; to dress with great neatness.<br><br><b>SPRUCE</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To dress ones self with affected neatness.<br><br><b>SPRUCE</b>, <i>n.</i> The fir-tree; a name given to a species of evergreen, the Pinus nigra, which is used in families to give flavor to beer. It is used by way of decoction, or in the essence.',
