  'Spurling-Line': {
    'id': 50257,
    'definition': '<b>SPURLING-LINE</b>, <i>n.</i> Among seamen, the line which forms the communication between the wheel and the tell-tale.',
  },
  'Spurn': {
    'id': 50258,
    'definition': '<b>SPURN</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [L., spur, kicking.]<br><br>1. To kick; to drive back or away, as with the foot.<br><br>2. To reject with disdain; to scorn to receive or accept. What multitudes of rational beings spurn the offers of eternal happiness!<br><br>3. To treat with contempt.<br><br><b>SPURN</b>, <i>v.i.</i><br><br>1. To manifest disdain in rejecting any thing; as, to spurn at the gracious offers of pardon.<br><br>2. To make contemptuous opposition; to manifest disdain in resistance.<br><br>Nay more, to spurn at your most royal image.<br><br>3. To kick or toss up the heels.<br><br>The drunken chairman in the kennel spurns.<br><br><b>SPURN</b>, <i>n.</i> Disdainful rejection; contemptuous treatment.<br><br>The insolence of office, and the spurns that patient merit of the unworthy takes.',
  },
