  'Stellated': {
    'id': 50677,
    'definition': '<b>STELLATE, STELLATED</b>, <i>a.</i> [L.]<br><br>1. Resembling a star; radiated.<br><br>2. In botany, stellate or verticillate leaves are when more leaves than two surround the stem in a whorl, or when they radiate like the spokes of a wheel, or like a star. A stellate bristle is when a little star of smaller hairs is affixed to the end applied also to the stigma. A stellate flower is a radiate flower.',
