  'Strew': {
    'id': 51145,
    'definition': '<b>STREW</b>, <i>v.t.</i> [This verb is written straw, strew, or strow; straw is nearly obsolete, and strow is obsolescent. Strew is generally used.]<br><br>1. To scatter; to spread by scattering; always applied to dry substances separable into parts or particles; as, to strew seed in beds; to strew sand on or over a floor; to strew flowers over a grave.<br><br>2. To spread by being scattered over.<br><br>The snow which does the top of Pindus strew.<br><br>Is thine alone the seed that strews the plain?<br><br>3. To scatter loosely.<br><br>And strewd his mangled limbs about the field.',
