    'definition': '<b>STRIPLING</b>, <i>n.</i> [from strip, stripe; primarily a tall slender youth, one that shoots up suddenly.] A youth in the state of adolescence, or just passing from boyhood to manhood; a lad.<br><br>And the king said, inquire thou whose son the stripling is. 1 Sam 18.',
