  'Sullied': {
    'id': 51781,
    'definition': '<b>SUL\'LIED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Soiled; tarnished; stained.',
  },
  'Sully': {
    'id': 51782,
    'definition': '<b>SUL\'LY</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To soil; to dirt; to spot; to tarnish.<br><br>And statues sullied yet with sacrilegious smoke.<br><br>2. To tarnish; to darken.<br><br>Let there be no spots to sully the brightness of this solemnity.<br><br>3. To stain; to tarnish; as the purity of reputation; as virtues sullied by slanders; character sullied by infamous vices.<br><br><b>SUL\'LY</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To be soiled or tarnished.<br><br>Silvering will sully and canker more than gilding.<br><br><b>SUL\'LY</b>, <i>n.</i> Soil, tarnish; spot.<br><br>A noble and triumphant merit breaks through little spots and sullies on his reputation.',
  },
