  },
  'Sulphore': {
    'id': 51787,
    'definition': '<b>SUL\'PHORE<br><br>SUL\'PHUR</b>, <i>n.</i> [L.] A simple combustible mineral substance, of a yellow color, brittle, insoluble in water, but fusible by heat. It is called also brimstone, that is, burn-stone, from its great combustibility. It burns with a blue flame and a peculiar suffocating odor. Sulphur native or prismatic is of two kinds, common and volcanic.',
