  'Swainmote': {
    'id': 52307,
    'definition': '<b>SWA\'INMOTE<br><br>SWAIRTH</b>, <i>n.</i> An apparition. [Not used in New England.',
  },
  'Swale': {
    'id': 52308,
    'definition': '<b>SWALE</b>, <i>n.</i> [probably from vale.] A local word in New England, signifying an interval or vale; a tract of low land.<br><br>1. In England, a shade.<br><br><b>SWALE</b>, <i>v.i.</i> To waste. [See <a href="dict://Sweal">Sweal</a>.]<br><br><b>SWALE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To dress a hog for bacon, by singeing or burning off his hair. [Local.]',
