  'Teasing': {
    'id': 53003,
    'definition': '<b>TE\'ASING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Combing; carding; scratching for the purpose of raising a nap; vexing with importunity.',
  },
  'Teat': {
    'id': 53004,
    'definition': '<b>TEAT<br><br>TEATHE</b>, <i>n.</i> The soil or fertility left on lands by feeding them. [Local.]<br><br><b>TEATHE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To feed and enrich by live stock. [Local.]',
  },
  'Techily': {
    'id': 53005,
    'definition': '<b>TECH\'ILY</b>, <i>adv.</i> [from techy, so written for touchy.]<br><br>Peevishly; fretfully; forwardly.',
  },
  'Techiness': {
    'id': 53006,
    'definition': '<b>TECH\'INESS</b>, <i>n.</i> Peevishness; fretfulness.',
  },
  'Technical': {
    'id': 53007,
    'definition': '<b>TECH\'NICAL</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. technicus; Gr. art, artifice; to fabricate, make or prepare.]<br><br>1. Pertaining to art or the arts. A technical word is a word that belongs properly or exclusively to an art; as the verb to smelt, belongs to metallurgy. So we say, technical phrases, technical language. Every artificer has his technical terms.<br><br>2. Belonging to a particular profession; as, the words of an indictment must be technical.<br><br>It is of the utmost importance clearly to understand the technical terms used by the eastern theologians.',
  },
  'Technicality': {
    'id': 53008,
    'definition': '<b>TECHNICAL\'ITY</b>, <i>n.</i> The quality or state of being technical or peculiar to the arts.',
  },
  'Technically': {
    'id': 53009,
    'definition': '<b>TECH\'NICALLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> In a technical manner; according to the signification of terms of art or the professions.',
  },
  'Technicalness': {
    'id': 53010,
    'definition': '<b>TECH\'NICALNESS<br><br>TECH\'NICS</b>, <i>n.</i> The doctrine of arts in general; such branches of learning as respect the arts.',
  },
  'Technological': {
    'id': 53011,
    'definition': '<b>TECHNOLOG\'ICAL</b>, <i>a.</i> [See <a href="dict://Technology">Technology</a>.]<br><br>1. Pertaining to technology.<br><br>2. Pertaining to the arts; as technological institutes.',
  },
  'Technologist': {
    'id': 53012,
    'definition': '<b>TECHNOL\'OGIST</b>, <i>n.</i> One who discourses or treats of arts, or of the terms of art.',
  },
  'Technology': {
    'id': 53013,
    'definition': '<b>TECHNOL\'OGY</b>, <i>n.</i> [Gr. art, and word or discourse.]<br><br>1. A description of arts; or a treatise on the arts.<br><br>2. An explanation of the terms of the arts.',
  },
  'Techy': {
    'id': 53014,
    'definition': '<b>TECH\'Y</b>, <i>a.</i> [so written for touchy.] Peevish; fretful; irritable. [More correctly touchy.]',
  },
  'Tecnnic': {
    'id': 53015,
    'definition': '<b>TECN\'NIC<br><br>TECTON\'IC</b>, <i>a.</i> [Gr. to fabricate.] Pertaining to building.',
  },
  'Ted': {
    'id': 53016,
    'definition': '<b>TED</b>, <i>v.t.</i> A spread; tedu, to distend. Among farmers, to spread; to turn new mowed grass from the swath, and scatter it for drying. [Local.]',
  },
  'Tedded': {
    'id': 53017,
    'definition': '<b>TED\'DED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Spread from the swath; as tedded grass.',
  },
  'Tedder': {
    'id': 53018,
    'definition': '<b>TED\'DER</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. A rope or chain by which an animal is tied that he may feed on the ground to the extent of the rope and no further. Hence the popular saying, a person has gone to the length of his tedder.<br><br>2. That by which one is restrained.<br><br><b>TED\'DER</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To tie with a tedder; to permit to feed to the length of a rope or chain.<br><br>1. To restrain to certain limits.<br><br>Te deum, a hymn to be sung in churches or on occasions of joy; so called from the first words.<br><br>Te deum was sung at St. Paul\'s after the victory.',
  },
  'Tede': {
    'id': 53019,
    'definition': '<b>TEDE</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. toeda.] A torch; a flambeau. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Tedious': {
    'id': 53020,
    'definition': '<b>TE\'DIOUS</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. toedium.]<br><br>1. Wearisome; tiresome from continuance, prolixity, or slowness which causes prolixity. We say, a man is tedious in relating a story; a minister is tedious in his sermon. We say also, a discourse is tedious, when it wearies by its length or dullness.<br><br>2. Slow; as a tedious course.',
  },
  'Tediously': {
    'id': 53021,
    'definition': '<b>TE\'DIOUSLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> In such a manner as to weary.',
  },
  'Tediousnes': {
    'id': 53022,
    'definition': '<b>TE\'DIOUSNES</b>, <i>n.</i> Wearisomeness by length of continuance or by prolixity; as the tediousness of an oration or argument.<br><br>1. Prolixity; length.<br><br>2. Tiresomeness; quality of wearying; as the tediousness of delay.<br><br>3. Slowness that wearies.',
  },
  'Tedium': {
    'id': 53023,
    'definition': '<b>TE\'DIUM</b>, <i>n.</i> [L. toedium.] Irksomeness; wearisomeness.',
  },
  'Teek': {
    'id': 53024,
    'definition': '<b>TEEK</b>, <i>n.</i> A tree of the East Indies, which furnishes an abundance of ship timber. The generic name given to it by Linne, is Tectona.',
  },
  'Teem': {
    'id': 53025,
    'definition': '<b>TEEM</b>, <i>v.i.<br><br></i> 1. To bring forth,as young.<br><br>If she must teem,<br><br>Create her child of spleen--<br><br>2. To be pregnant; to conceive; to engender young.<br><br>Teeming buds and cheerful greens appear.<br><br>3. To be full; to be charged; as a breeding animal; to be prolific. Every head teems with politics.<br><br>4. To bring forth; to produce, particularly in abundance. The earth teems with fruits; the sea teems with fishes.<br><br><b>TEEM</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To produce; to bring forth.<br><br>What\'s the newest grief?<br><br>Each minute teems a new one.<br><br>[This transitive sense is not common.]<br><br>1. To pour. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Teemer': {
    'id': 53026,
    'definition': '<b>TEE\'MER</b>, <i>n.</i> One that brings forth young.',
  },
  'Teemful': {
    'id': 53027,
    'definition': '<b>TEE\'MFUL</b>, <i>a.</i> Pregnant; prolific.<br><br>1. Brimful.',
  },
  'Teeming': {
    'id': 53028,
    'definition': '<b>TEE\'MING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Producing young.',
  },
  'Teemless': {
    'id': 53029,
    'definition': '<b>TEE\'MLESS</b>, <i>a.</i> Not fruitful or prolific; barren; as the teemless earth.',
  },
  'Teen': {
    'id': 53030,
    'definition': '<b>TEEN</b>, <i>n.</i> [infra.] Grief; sorrow. [Not in use.]<br><br><b>TEEN</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To excite; to provoke., [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Teens': {
    'id': 53031,
    'definition': '<b>TEENS</b>, <i>n.</i> [from teen, ten.] The years of one\'s age reckoned by the termination teen. These years begin with thirteen, and end with nineteen. Miss is in her teens.',
  },
  'Teeth': {
    'id': 53032,
    'definition': '<b>TEETH</b>, <i>plu.</i> of tooth, which see.<br><br>In the teeth, directly; in direct opposition; in front.<br><br>Nor strive with all the tempest in my teeth.<br><br><b>TEETH</b>, <i>v.i.</i> [from the noun.] To breed teeth.',
  },
  'Teething': {
    'id': 53033,
    'definition': '<b>TEE\'THING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Breeding teeth; undergoing dentition.<br><br><b>TEE\'THING</b>, <i>n.</i> The operation or process of the first growth of teeth, or the process by which they make their way through the gums, called dentition.',
  },
  'Tegular': {
    'id': 53034,
    'definition': '<b>TEG\'ULAR</b>, <i>a.</i> [L. tegula, a tile, from tego, to cover or make close.] Pertaining to a tile; resembling a tile; consisting of tiles.',
  },
  'Tegularly': {
    'id': 53035,
    'definition': '<b>TEG\'ULARLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> In the manner of tiles on a roof.',
