  'Thievery': {
    'id': 53505,
    'definition': '<b>THIE\'VERY</b>, <i>n.</i> The practice of stealing; theft. [See <a href="dict://Theft">Theft</a>.]<br><br>Among the Spartans, thievery was a practice morally good and honest.<br><br>1. That which is stolen.',
  },
  'Thievish': {
    'id': 53506,
    'definition': '<b>THIE\'VISH</b>, <i>a.</i> Given to stealing; addicted to the practice of theft; as a thievish boy.<br><br>Or with a base and boist\'rous sword enforce<br><br>A thievish living on the common road.<br><br>1. Secret; sly; acting by stealth; as thievish minutes.<br><br>2. Partaking of the nature of theft; as a thievish practice.',
  },
  'Thievishly': {
    'id': 53507,
    'definition': '<b>THIE\'VISHLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> In a thievish manner; by theft.',
