    'definition': '<br>UNBILT, a. Not yet built; not erected.',
  },
  'Unbind': {
    'id': 55703,
    'definition': '<b>UNBIND</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To untie; to remove a band from; to unfasten; to loose; to set free from shackles. Unbind your fillets; unbind the prisoner\'s arms; unbind the load.',
  },
  'Unbishop': {
