  'Underleaf': {
    'id': 56234,
    'definition': '<b>UNDERLE\'AF</b>, <i>n.</i> A sort of apple good for cider.',
  },
  'Underlet': {
    'id': 56235,
    'definition': '<b>UNDERLET\'</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To let below the value.<br><br>2. To let or lease, as a lessee or tenant; to let under a lease.<br><br>It is a matter of much importance - that the tenant should have power to underlet his farms.',
  },
  'Underletter': {
