    'definition': '<b>UNFEE\'LINGNESS</b>, <i>n.</i> Insensibility; harness of heart; cruelty.',
  },
  'Unfeigned': {
    'id': 56635,
    'definition': '<b>UNFEIGNED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not feigned; not counterfeit; not hypocritical; real; sincere; as unfeigned piety to God; unfeigned love to man.',
  },
  'Unfeignedly': {
    'id': 56636,
    'definition': '<b>UNFEIGNEDLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> Without hypocrisy; really; sincerely.<br><br>He pardoneth all them that truly repent, and unfeignedly believe his holy gospel.',
  },
  'Unfelicitating': {
    'id': 56637,
    'definition': '<b>UNFELIC\'ITATING</b>, <i>a.</i> Not producing felicity. [Unusual.]',
  },
  'Unfellowed': {
    'id': 56638,
    'definition': '<b>UNFEL\'LOWED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not matched.',
  },
  'Unfelt': {
    'id': 56639,
    'definition': '<b>UNFELT\'</b>, <i>a.</i> Not felt; not perceived.',
  },
  'Unfence': {
    'id': 56640,
    'definition': '<b>UNFENCE</b>, <i>v.t.</i> unfens\'. To strip of fence; to remove a fence from.',
  },
  'Unfenced': {
    'id': 56641,
    'definition': '<b>UNFEN\'CED</b>, <i>pp.<br><br></i> 1. Deprived of a fence.<br><br>2. a. Not fenced; not inclosed; defenseless; as a tract of land unfenced.',
  },
  'Unfermented': {
    'id': 56642,
    'definition': '<b>UNFERMENT\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i><br><br>1. Not fermented; not having undergone the process of fermentation; as liquor.<br><br>2. Not leavened; as bread.',
  },
  'Unfertile': {
    'id': 56643,
    'definition': '<b>UNFER\'TILE</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not fertile; not rich; not having the qualities necessary to the production of good crops.<br><br>2. Barren; unfruitful; bare; waste.<br><br>3. Not prolific.<br><br>[This word is not obsolete, but infertile is much used instead of it.]',
  },
  'Unfethered': {
    'id': 56644,
    'definition': '<b>UNFETH\'ERED</b>, <i>a.</i> Having no feathers; unfledged; implumous; naked of feathers.',
  },
  'Unfetter': {
    'id': 56645,
    'definition': '<b>UNFET\'TER</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To loose from fetters; to unchain; to unshackle.<br><br>2. To free from restraint; to set at liberty; as, to unfetter the mind.',
  },
  'Unfettered': {
    'id': 56646,
    'definition': '<b>UNFET\'TERED</b>, <i>pp.</i><br><br>1. Unchained; unshackled; freed from restraint.<br><br>2. a. Not restrained.',
  },
  'Unfettering': {
    'id': 56647,
    'definition': '<b>UNFET\'TERING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Unchaining; setting free from restraint.',
  },
  'Unfigured': {
    'id': 56648,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIG\'URED</b>, <i>a.</i> Representing no animal form.',
  },
  'Unfilial': {
    'id': 56649,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIL\'IAL</b>, <i>a.</i> Unsuitable to a son or child; undutiful; not becoming a child.',
  },
  'Unfilled': {
    'id': 56650,
    'definition': '<b>UNFILL\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not filled; not fully supplied.',
  },
  'Unfinished': {
    'id': 56651,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIN\'ISHED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not finished; not complete; not brought to an end; imperfect; wanting the last hand or touch; as an unfinished house; an unfinished painting.',
  },
  'Unfired': {
    'id': 56652,
    'definition': '<b>UNFI\'RED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not fired; not inflamed.',
  },
  'Unfirm': {
    'id': 56653,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIRM\'</b>, <i>a.</i> [See <a href="dict://Firm">Firm</a>.]<br><br>1. Not firm; weak; feeble; infirm.<br><br>[Note. When we speak of the weakness of the human frame, we use infirm. When we speak of the weakness of other things, as a bridge, wall and the like, we say, it is unfirm.]<br><br>2. Not stable; not well fixed.<br><br>With feet unfirm.',
  },
  'Unfirmness': {
    'id': 56654,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIRM\'NESS</b>, <i>n.</i> A weak state; instability.',
  },
  'Unfit': {
    'id': 56655,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIT\'</b>, <i>a.</i><br><br>1. Not fit; improper; unsuitable.<br><br>2. Unqualified; as a man unfit for an office.<br><br><b>UNFIT\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i><br><br>1. To disable; to make unsuitable; to deprive of the strength, skill or proper qualities for any thing. Sickness unfits a man for labor.<br><br>2. To disqualify; to deprive of the moral or mental qualities necessary for any thing. Sin unfits us for the society of holy beings.',
  },
  'Unfitly': {
    'id': 56656,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIT\'LY</b>, <i>adv.</i> Not properly; unsuitably.',
  },
  'Unfitness': {
    'id': 56657,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIT\'NESS</b>, <i>n.<br><br></i> 1. Want of suitable powers or qualifications, physical or moral; as the unfitness of a sick man for labor, or of an ignorant man for office; the unfitness of sinners for the enjoyments of heaven.<br><br>2. Want of propriety or adaptation to character or place; as unfitness of behavior or of dress.',
  },
  'Unfitted': {
    'id': 56658,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIT\'TED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Rendered unsuitable; disqualified.',
  },
  'Unfitting': {
    'id': 56659,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIT\'TING</b>, <i>ppr.<br><br></i> 1. Rendering unsuitable; disqualifying.<br><br>2. a. Improper; becoming.',
  },
  'Unfix': {
    'id': 56660,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIX\'</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To loosen from any fastening; to detach from any thing that holds; to unsettle; to unhinge; as, to unfix the mind or affections.<br><br>2. To make fluid; to dissolve.<br><br>Nor can the rising sun unfix their frosts.',
  },
  'Unfixed': {
    'id': 56661,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIX\'ED</b>, <i>pp.<br><br></i> 1. Unsettled; loosened.<br><br>2. a. Wandering; erratic; inconstant; having no settled habitation.<br><br>3. Having no settled view or object of pursuit.',
  },
  'Unfixing': {
    'id': 56662,
    'definition': '<b>UNFIX\'ING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Unsettling; loosening.',
  },
  'Unflagging': {
    'id': 56663,
    'definition': '<b>UNFLAG\'GING</b>, <i>a.</i> Not flagging; not drooping; maintaining strength or spirit.',
  },
  'Unflattered': {
    'id': 56664,
    'definition': '<b>UNFLAT\'TERED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not flattered.',
  },
  'Unflattering': {
    'id': 56665,
    'definition': '<b>UNFLAT\'TERING</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not flattering; not gratifying with obsequious behavior; not coloring the truth to please.<br><br>2. Not affording a favorable prospect; as, the weather is unflattering.',
  },
  'Unfledged': {
    'id': 56666,
    'definition': '<b>UNFLEDG\'ED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not yet furnished with feathers; implumous; as an unfledged bird.<br><br>2. Young; not having attained to full growth.',
  },
  'Unfleshed': {
    'id': 56667,
    'definition': '<b>UNFLESH\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not fleshed; not seasoned to blood; raw; as an unfleshed hound; unfleshed valor.',
  },
  'Unfoiled': {
    'id': 56668,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOIL\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not vanquished; not defeated.',
  },
  'Unfold': {
    'id': 56669,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOLD</b>, <i>v.t<br><br></i> 1. To open folds; to expand; to spread out.<br><br>2. To open any thing covered or close; to lay open to view or contemplation; to disclose; to reveal; as, to unfold one\'s designs; to unfold the principles of a science.<br><br>3. To declare; to tell; to disclose.<br><br>Unfold the passion of my love.<br><br>4. To display; as, to unfold the works of creation.<br><br>5. To release from a fold or pen; as, to unfold sheep.',
  },
  'Unfolded': {
    'id': 56670,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOLDED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Opened; expanded; revealed; displayed; released from a fold.',
  },
  'Unfolding': {
    'id': 56671,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOLDING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Opening; expanding; disclosing; displaying; releasing from a fold.<br><br><b>UNFOLDING</b>, <i>n.</i> The act of expanding, displaying or disclosing; disclosure.',
  },
  'Unfool': {
    'id': 56672,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOOL\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To restore from folly. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Unforbearing': {
    'id': 56673,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORBEARING</b>, <i>a.</i> Not forbearing.',
  },
  'Unforbid': {
    'id': 56674,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORBID\',<br><br>UNFORBID\'DEN</b>, <i>a.</i><br><br>1. Not forbid; not prohibited; applied to persons.<br><br>2. Allowed; permitted; legal; applied to things.',
  },
  'Unforbiddenness': {
    'id': 56675,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORBID\'DENNESS</b>, <i>n.</i> The state of being unforbidden. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Unforced': {
    'id': 56676,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORCED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not forced; not compelled; not constrained.<br><br>2. Not urged or impelled.<br><br>3. Not feigned; not heightened; natural as unforced passions; unforced expressions of joy.<br><br>4. Not violent; easy; gradual; as an easy and unforced ascent.<br><br>5. Easy; natural; as an unforced posture.',
  },
  'Unforcible': {
    'id': 56677,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORCIBLE</b>, <i>a.</i> Wanting force or strength; as an unforcible expression.',
  },
  'Unfordable': {
    'id': 56678,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORDABLE</b>, <i>a.</i> Not fordable; that cannot be forded, or passed by wading; as an unfordable river.',
  },
  'Unforeboding': {
    'id': 56679,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOREBO\'DING</b>, <i>a.</i> Giving no omens.',
  },
  'Unforeknown': {
    'id': 56680,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOREKNOWN</b>, <i>a.</i> Not previously known or foreseen.',
  },
  'Unforeseeable': {
    'id': 56681,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORESEE\'ABLE</b>, <i>a.</i> That cannot be foreseen. [A bad word and not in use.]',
  },
  'Unforeseen': {
    'id': 56682,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORESEE\'N</b>, <i>a.</i> Not foreseen; not foreknown.',
  },
  'Unforeskinned': {
    'id': 56683,
    'definition': '<b>UNFO\'RESKINNED</b>, <i>a.</i> Circumcised. [Bad.]',
  },
  'Unforetold': {
    'id': 56684,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORETOLD</b>, <i>a.</i> Not predicted.',
  },
  'Unforewarned': {
    'id': 56685,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOREWARN\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i> a. [See <a href="dict://Warn">Warn</a>.] Not previously warned or admonished.',
  },
  'Unforfeited': {
    'id': 56686,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOR\'FEITED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not forfeited.',
  },
  'Unforgiven': {
    'id': 56687,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORGIV\'EN</b>, <i>a.</i> Not forgiven; not pardoned.',
  },
  'Unforgiving': {
    'id': 56688,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORGIV\'ING</b>, <i>a.</i> Not forgiving; not disposed to overlook or pardon offenses; implacable.',
  },
  'Unforgot': {
    'id': 56689,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORGOT\'<br><br>UNFORGOT\'TEN</b>, <i>a.</i><br><br>1. Not forgot; not lost to memory.<br><br>2. Not overlooked; not neglected.',
  },
  'Unform': {
    'id': 56690,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORM\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To destroy; to unmake; to decompose or resolve into parts.',
  },
  'Unformed': {
    'id': 56691,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORM\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not molded into regular shape; as unformed matter.',
  },
  'Unforsaken': {
    'id': 56692,
    'definition': '<b>UNFORSA\'KEN</b>, <i>a.</i> Not forsaken; not deserted; not entirely neglected.',
  },
  'Unfortified': {
    'id': 56693,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOR\'TIFIED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not fortified; not secured from attack by walls or mounds.<br><br>2. Not guarded; not strengthened against temptations or trials; weak; exposed; defenseless; as an unfortified mind.<br><br>3. Wanting securities or means of defense.',
  },
  'Unfortunate': {
    'id': 56694,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOR\'TUNATE</b>, <i>a.</i> Not successful; not prosperous; as an unfortunate adventure; an unfortunate voyage; unfortunate attempts; an unfortunate man; an unfortunate commander; unfortunate business.',
  },
  'Unfortunately': {
    'id': 56695,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOR\'TUNATELY</b>, <i>adv.</i> Without success; unsuccessfully; unhappily. the scheme unfortunately miscarried.',
  },
  'Unfortunateness': {
    'id': 56696,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOR\'TUNATENESS</b>, <i>n.</i> Ill luck; ill fortune; fortune; failure of success.',
  },
  'Unfostered': {
    'id': 56697,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOS\'TERED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not fostered; not nourished.<br><br>2. Not countenanced by favor; not patronized.',
  },
  'Unfought': {
    'id': 56698,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOUGHT</b>, <i>a.</i> unfaut\'. Not fought.',
  },
  'Unfouled': {
    'id': 56699,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOUL\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not fouled; not polluted; not soiled; not corrupted; pure.',
  },
  'Unfound': {
    'id': 56700,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOUND\'</b>, <i>a.</i> Not found; not met with.',
  },
  'Unfounded': {
    'id': 56701,
    'definition': '<b>UNFOUND\'ED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not founded; not built or established.<br><br>2. Having no foundation; vain; idle; as unfounded expectations.',
  },
  'Unframable': {
    'id': 56702,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRA\'MABLE</b>, <i>a.</i> Not to be framed or molded. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Unframableness': {
    'id': 56703,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRA\'MABLENESS</b>, <i>n.</i> The quality of not being framable. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Unframed': {
    'id': 56704,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRA\'MED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not framed; not fitted for erection; as unframed timber.<br>2. Not formed; not constructed; not fashioned.',
  },
  'Unfraternal': {
    'id': 56705,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRATERN\'AL</b>, <i>a.</i> Not brotherly.',
  },
  'Unfree': {
    'id': 56706,
    'definition': '<b>UNFREE\'</b>, <i>a.</i> Not free; as unfree peasants.',
  },
  'Unfrequency': {
    'id': 56707,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRE\'QUENCY</b>, <i>n.</i> The state of being unfrequent.',
  },
  'Unfrequent': {
    'id': 56708,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRE\'QUENT</b>, <i>a.</i> Not frequent; not common; not happening often; infrequent.<br><br><b>UNFRE\'QUENT</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To cease to frequent. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Unfrequented': {
    'id': 56709,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRE\'QUENTED</b>, <i>a.</i> Rarely visited; seldom resorted to by human beings; as an unfrequented place or forest.',
  },
  'Unfrequently': {
    'id': 56710,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRE\'QUENTLY</b>, <i>adv.</i> Not often; seldom.',
  },
  'Unfriable': {
    'id': 56711,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRI\'ABLE</b>, <i>a.</i> Not easily crumbled.',
  },
  'Unfriended': {
    'id': 56712,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRIENDED</b>, <i>a.</i> unfrend\'ed. Wanting friends; not countenanced or supported.',
  },
  'Unfriendliness': {
    'id': 56713,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRIEND\'LINESS</b>, <i>n.</i> Want of kindness; disfavor.',
  },
  'Unfriendly': {
    'id': 56714,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRIEND\'LY</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not friendly; not kind or benevolent; as an unfriendly neighbor.<br><br>2. Not favorable; not adapted to promote or support any object; as weather unfriendly to health.',
  },
  'Unfrock': {
    'id': 56715,
    'definition': '<b>UNFROCK\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To divest.',
  },
  'Unfrozen': {
    'id': 56716,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRO\'ZEN</b>, <i>a.</i> Not frozen; not congealed.',
  },
  'Unfrugal': {
    'id': 56717,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRU\'GAL</b>, <i>a.</i> Not frugal; not saving or economical.',
  },
  'Unfruitful': {
    'id': 56718,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRUITFUL</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not producing fruit; barren; as an unfruitful tree.<br><br>2. Not producing off-spring; not prolific; barren; as an unfruitful female.<br><br>3. Not producing good effects or works; as an unfruitful life.<br><br>4. Unproductive; not fertile; as an unfruitful soil.',
  },
  'Unfruitfulness': {
    'id': 56719,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRUITFULNESS</b>, <i>n.</i> Barrenness; infecundity; unproductiveness; applied to persons or things.',
  },
  'Unfrustrable': {
    'id': 56720,
    'definition': '<b>UNFRUS\'TRABLE</b>, <i>a.</i> That cannot be frustrated.',
  },
  'Unfulfilled': {
    'id': 56721,
    'definition': '<b>UNFULFILL\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not fulfilled; not accomplished; as a prophecy or prediction unfulfilled.',
  },
  'Unfumed': {
    'id': 56722,
    'definition': '<b>UNFU\'MED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not fumigated.<br><br>2. Not exhaling smoke; not burnt.',
  },
  'Unfunded': {
    'id': 56723,
    'definition': '<b>UNFUND\'ED</b>, <i>a.</i> Not funded; having no permanent funds for the payment of its interest; as an unfunded debt.',
  },
  'Unfurl': {
    'id': 56724,
    'definition': '<b>UNFURL\'</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To loose and unfold; to expand; to open or spread; as, to unfurl sails.',
  },
  'Unfurled': {
    'id': 56725,
    'definition': '<b>UNFURL\'ED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Unfolded; expanded.',
  },
  'Unfurling': {
    'id': 56726,
    'definition': '<b>UNFURL\'ING</b>, <i>ppr.</i> Unfolding; spreading.',
  },
  'Unfurnish': {
    'id': 56727,
    'definition': '<b>UNFUR\'NISH</b>, <i>v.t.<br><br></i> 1. To strip of furniture; to divest; to strip.<br><br>2. To leave naked.',
  },
  'Unfurnished': {
    'id': 56728,
    'definition': '<b>UNFUR\'NISHED</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Not furnished; not supplied with furniture; as an unfurnished room or house.<br><br>2. Unsupplied with necessaries or ornaments.<br><br>3. Empty; not supplied.',
  },
  'Unfused': {
    'id': 56729,
    'definition': '<b>UNFU\'SED</b>, <i>a.</i> s as z. Not fused; not melted.',
  },
  'Unfusible': {
    'id': 56730,
    'definition': '<b>UNFU\'SIBLE</b>, <i>a.</i> s as z. Infusible. [The latter word is generally used.]',
  },
  'Ungainable': {
    'id': 56731,
    'definition': '<b>UNGA\'INABLE</b>, <i>a.</i> That cannot be gained. [Little used.]',
  },
  'Ungainful': {
    'id': 56732,
    'definition': '<b>UNGA\'INFUL</b>, <i>a.</i> Unprofitable; not producing gain.',
  },
  'Ungainly': {
    'id': 56733,
    'definition': '<b>UNGA\'INLY</b>, <i>a.</i> Not expert or dextrous; clumsy; awkward; uncouth; as an ungainly strut in walking.<br><br>[I believe ungain is not used.]',
  },
  'Ungalled': {
