  'Unruliness': {
    'id': 57733,
    'definition': '<b>UNRU\'LINESS</b>, <i>n.</i> [from unruly.]<br><br>1. Disregard of restraint; licentiousness; turbulence; as the unruliness of men, or of their passions.<br><br>2. The disposition of a beast to break over fences and wander from an inclosure; the practice of breaking or leaping over fences.',
  },
  'Unruly': {
    'id': 57734,
    'definition': '<b>UNRU\'LY</b>, <i>a.<br><br></i> 1. Disregarding restraint; licentious; disposed to violate laws; turbulent; ungovernable; as an unruly youth.<br><br>The tongue can no man tame; it is an unruly evil. James 4.<br><br>2. Accustomed to break over fences and escape from inclosures; apt to break or leap fences; as an unruly ox.<br><br>The owner of the unruly ox paid a sum of money, as a civil penalty for the ransom of his life.',
  },
