  'Wallow': {
    'id': 59538,
    'definition': '<b>WALLOW</b>, <i>v.i.</i> [L., G. This verb seems to be connected with well, walk, &c.]<br><br>1. To roll ones body on the earth, in mire, or on other substance; to tumble and roll in water. Swine wallow in the mire.<br><br>2. To move heavily and clumsily.<br><br>Part huge of bulk, wallowing unwieldy, enormous in their gait, tempest the ocean. [Unusual.]<br><br>3. To live in filth or gross vice; as man wallowing in his native impurity.<br><br><b>WALLOW</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To roll ones body.<br><br>Wallow thyself in ashes. Jer 6.<br><br><b>WALLOW</b>, <i>n.</i> A kind of rolling walk.',
