  'Wantonness': {
    'id': 59576,
    'definition': '<b>WANTONNESS</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. Sportiveness; gaiety; frolicsomeness; waggery.<br><br>--As sad as night, only for wantonness.<br><br>2. Licentiousness; negligence of restraint.<br><br>The tumults threatened to abuse all acts of grace, and turn them into wantonness.<br><br>3. Lasciviousness; lewdness. Rom 8. II Peter 2.',
