    'id': 59599,
    'definition': '<b>WARDEN</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. A keeper; a guardian.<br><br>2. An officer who keeps or guards; a keeper; as the warden of the fleet or fleet prison.<br><br>3. A large pear.<br><br>Warden of the cinque ports, in England, an officer or magistrate who has the jurisdiction of a port or haven. There are five such ports.<br><br>Warden of a university, is the master or president.',
