    'id': 59674,
    'definition': '<b>WASH-BOARD</b>, <i>n.</i> [wash and board.]<br><br>1. A broad thin plank, fixed occasionally on the top of a boat or other small vessels side, to prevent the sea from breaking over; also, a piece of plank on the sill of a lower deck port for the same purpose.<br><br>2. A board in a room, next to the floor.',
