  'Wasteness': {
    'id': 59700,
    'definition': '<b>WASTENESS</b>, <i>n.</i> A desolate state; solitude.<br><br>That day is a day of wrath, a day of trouble and distress, a day of wasteness. Zep 1.',
  },
  'Waster': {
    'id': 59701,
    'definition': '<b>WASTER</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. One who is prodigal; one who squanders property; one who consumes extravagantly or without use.<br><br>He also that is slothful in his work, is brother to him who is a great waster. Prov 18.<br><br>Sconces are great wasters of candles.<br><br>2. A kind of cudgel.',
