  'Water-Hammer': {
    'id': 59750,
    'definition': '<b>WATER-HAMMER</b>, <i>n.</i> A column of water in a vacuum, which not being supported as in the air, falls against the end of the vessel with a peculiar noise. It may be formed by corking a vessel of water while it is boiling. The vapor condensing as it cools, a vacuum is formed.',
