    'definition': '<b>WEIVE</b>, <i>for</i> waive. [Not in use.]',
  },
  'Welaway': {
    'id': 59998,
    'definition': '<b>WELAWAY</b>, <i>an</i> exclamation expressive of grief or sorrow, equivalent to alas. It is a compound of Sax. Wa, wo and la, oh. The original is wa-la, which is doubtless the origin of our common exclamation, O la, and to this, wa, wo, is added. The true orthography would be wa la wa. But the word is, I believe, wholly obsolete.',
  },
  'Welcome': {
    'id': 59999,
    'definition': '<b>WELCOME</b>, <i>a.</i><br><br>1. Received with gladness; admitted willingly to the house, entertainment and company; as a welcome guest.<br><br>2. Grateful; pleasing; as a welcome present; welcome news.<br><br>3. Free to have or enjoy gratuitously. You are welcome to the use of my library.<br><br>To bid welcome, to receive with professions of kindness.<br><br><b>WELCOME</b>, <i>is</i> used elliptically for you are welcome.<br><br>Welcome, great monarch, to your own.<br><br>Welcome to our house, an herb.<br><br><b>WELCOME</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. Salutation of a new comer.<br><br>Welcome ever smiles--<br><br>2. Kind reception of a guest or new comer. We entered the house and found a ready welcome.<br><br>Truth finds an entrance and a welcome too.<br><br><b>WELCOME</b>, <i>v.t.</i> To salute a new comer with kindness; or to receive and entertain hospitable, gratuitously and cheerfully.<br><br>Thus we salute thee with our early song, and welcome thee, and wish thee long.',
  },
  'Welcomed': {
    'id': 60000,
    'definition': '<b>WELCOMED</b>, <i>pp.</i> Received with gladness and kindness.',
  },
  'Welcomely': {
    'id': 60001,
    'definition': '<b>WELCOMELY</b>, <i>adv.</i> In a welcome manner.',
  },
  'Welcomeness': {
