  'Windiness': {
    'id': 60476,
    'definition': '<b>WINDINESS</b>, <i>n.</i> [from windey.]<br><br>1. The state of being windy or tempestuous; as the windiness of the weather or season.<br><br>2. Fullness of wind; flatulence.<br><br>3. Tendency to generate wind; as the windiness of vegetables.<br><br>4. Tumor; puffiness.<br><br>The swelling windiness of much knowledge.',
  },
  'Winding': {
    'id': 60477,
    'definition': '<b>WINDING</b>, <i>ppr.</i><br><br>1. Turning; binding about; bending.<br><br>2. a. Bending; twisting from a direct line or an even surface.<br><br><b>WINDING</b>, <i>n.</i><br><br>1. A turn or turning; a bend; flexure; meander; as the windings of a road or stream.<br><br>2. A call by the boastswains whistle.',
